"""Source-authored bilingual manuscript. Review scope: depth-review-2026-10-20/REPORT.md."""
from model import p, ref, block, section

PART = dict(title=p('金錢服務經營者的系統及管控措施（二）：打擊洗錢及恐怖分子資金籌集的管控範疇', 'MSO systems and controls (ii): AML/CFT control areas'),
intro=p('本部分按實際管控範疇整理：識別客戶及背後人士、判定審查程度、監察交易、篩查制裁，以及處理匯款和交付渠道。規定須連同觸發條件及例外一起記。', 'This part covers operational controls: identifying customers and the people behind them, setting due-diligence intensity, monitoring, sanctions screening, transfers and delivery channels. Learn each requirement with its trigger and exceptions.'), sections=[
section('cdd', '客戶盡職審查：定義及四項措施', 'Customer due diligence: definition and four measures', [
    block('四項基本措施', 'Four basic measures', [
        ('客戶盡職審查（CDD）的第一項，是先確認你在跟誰做生意，再用可靠、獨立來源的文件、數據或資料，核實這個人或機構的身分。不能只聽對方自報姓名，便當成已經完成核實。', 'The first customer due diligence (CDD) measure is to identify who you are dealing with, and then to verify that identity using documents, data or information from a reliable, independent source. A name the customer simply states is not, by itself, completed verification.'),
        ('如果有實益擁有人，還要識別這個人，並採取合理措施核實其身分，使機構信納自己知道對方是誰。對於法人及信託，還須了解擁有權及控制結構，不能只停在表面上的公司名稱。', 'Where there is a beneficial owner, identify that person and take reasonable identity-verification measures, so the MSO is satisfied it knows who that person is. For legal persons and trusts, also understand the ownership and control structures; do not stop at the name on the surface.'),
        ('還要取得這段業務關係的目的，以及擬具有的性質。如果這些已經顯而易見，便不必另行再取一次。客戶不是自然人時，還須了解其業務性質。', 'Also obtain information on the purpose and intended nature of the relationship, unless that is already obvious. Where the customer is not a natural person, also understand the nature of its business.'),
        ('如果有人代表客戶行事，須識別這名代表，並採取合理措施核實其身分，另外還要核實其授權。代表的身分，和這個人是否真的獲授權，是兩件都要處理的事，缺一不可。例如：櫃台來人出示公司名片，只能說明這個人是誰，並不能單憑名片證明公司已授權他簽約或發指示。', 'If someone acts for the customer, identify that representative, take reasonable measures to verify the representative’s identity, and separately verify authority. Identity and authorisation are two distinct requirements, and both must be dealt with. For example: a business card produced at the counter may help show who the person is, but it does not, by itself, prove that the company has authorised that person to sign or give instructions.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.1.1–4.1.5、4.6.1段', '¶4.1.1–4.1.5, 4.6.1', 'The following are CDD measures applicable to an MSO'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('客戶的界定', 'Who is the customer', [
        ('「客戶」通常是與機構建立業務關係的一方，或機構為其執行交易的一方，一般不包括交易裡的第三方。例如：對匯出機構而言，只是收款、而且與機構沒有其他關係的受款人，並不會自動成為該機構的客戶。', 'The “customer” is generally the party with whom the relationship is established, or for whom the transaction is carried out, and usually excludes third parties to the transaction. For example: a beneficiary of an outward transfer who has no other relationship with the ordering MSO is not automatically that MSO’s customer.'),
        ('與法人建立關係時，須識別該法人本身。只識別到櫃台辦理手續的個人，並不能代替識別他所代表的公司。例如：職員只核對了來辦手續的張先生的身分證，卻沒有核實他所代表的有限公司，這樣並未完成對法人客戶的識別。', 'When a relationship is established with a legal person, identify the legal-person customer itself. Identifying the individual at the counter does not substitute for identifying the company that person represents. For example: checking only Mr Cheung’s identity card, without verifying the limited company he represents, does not complete identification of the legal-person customer.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.1.4–4.1.5段', '¶4.1.4–4.1.5', 'generally excludes the third parties'),
        ref('07', '附錄第(3)部分，第5頁', 'Appendix (3), p.5', 'treated a PPTA as the customer'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('triggers', 'CDD觸發條件、金額及相連交易', 'CDD triggers, thresholds and linked transactions', [
    block('必須執行的情況', 'When CDD is required', [
        ('建立業務關係之前，不論金額多少，都必須先做客戶盡職審查。業務關係是具有持續性的業務、專業或商業關係，或者機構在首次接觸潛在客戶時，預期會具有這種持續性。一次過的小額兌換，如果機構並不預期會持續往來，通常還不是這裡所說的業務關係。', 'Perform CDD before establishing a business relationship, regardless of the amount. A business relationship has an element of duration, or is expected to have one when the potential customer first contacts the MSO. A one-off low-value exchange, where no continuing relationship is expected, is not usually a business relationship of this kind.'),
        ('非經常交易，是與沒有業務關係的客戶進行的交易，並且有自己的金額觸發點。一般非經常交易達港幣120,000元或等值外幣、電傳轉帳達港幣8,000元或等值，以及虛擬資產轉帳涉及價值不少於港幣8,000元，均須在執行前完成客戶盡職審查。例如：一筆沒有業務關係的兌換剛好是港幣120,000元，已觸發一般非經常交易的CDD；不要把它跟電傳轉帳的港幣8,000元門檻混在一起。', 'An occasional transaction is a transaction with a customer who has no business relationship with the MSO, and it has its own amount triggers. CDD is required before general occasional transactions of at least HK$120,000 or equivalent, wire transfers of at least HK$8,000 or equivalent, and virtual-asset transfers worth at least HK$8,000. In each case, the CDD must be completed before the transaction is carried out. For example: a one-off exchange of exactly HK$120,000 with a customer who has no business relationship already triggers general occasional-transaction CDD. Do not mix that figure up with the HK$8,000 wire-transfer threshold.'),
        ('計算門檻時，單筆交易要算，機構認為看來相連的多筆交易也要一併計算。同一受款人在短時間內，從一個或多個來源收到付款，或客戶經常向同一或多個目的地轉帳，都可以構成相連的線索。例如：兩筆看來相連的付款，即使每一筆都低於一般非經常交易的港幣120,000元門檻，合併計算後仍可能達標。', 'When applying a threshold, count a single operation, and also operations that appear to the MSO to be linked. Payments to the same recipient from one or more sources over a short period, or regular transfers to the same or several destinations, may indicate linkage. For example: two payments that appear linked can still be counted together, and may meet the general occasional-transaction threshold of HK$120,000 even if each payment is below that figure.'),
        ('另外兩種情況也會觸發CDD，而且不受金額門檻限制：懷疑客戶或戶口涉及洗錢或恐怖分子資金籌集；或者懷疑原有識別或核實資料的真實性或充分性。即使金額很小，只要出現這類懷疑或疑問，仍須做審查。', 'Two further situations also trigger CDD, and they are not subject to a monetary threshold: suspicion of money laundering or terrorist financing involving the customer or the account; or doubts about the truth or adequacy of existing identification or verification information. Even a small amount still requires CDD if that suspicion or those doubts arise.'),
        ('不要只記得一般非經常交易的港幣120,000元門檻。非電傳的對外匯款如果達港幣8,000元，另有一套發款人核實及紀錄要求，會在本部分「匯款」一節說明。', 'Do not rely solely on the general occasional-transaction threshold of HK$120,000. Non-wire outward remittances of at least HK$8,000 have separate originator-verification and record requirements, which are explained under Remittances later in this Part.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.2.1–4.2.5、11.3段', '¶4.2.1–4.2.5, 11.3', 'whether the transaction is carried out in a single operation'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('第三方現金交易', 'Third-party cash transactions', [
        ('如果不是戶口授權名單上的人，代為存入達港幣120,000元的現金，機構應要求其身分文件並保留副本，以便持續監察。與客戶風險背景不符的大額現金，須特別留意。', 'For a cash transaction of at least HK$120,000 by a person who is not on the account mandate, request and copy that person’s identity document for ongoing monitoring. Large cash amounts that are inconsistent with the customer’s risk profile require particular attention.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.2.6段', '¶4.2.6', 'whose name does not appear on the mandate'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('identity', '身分資料：自然人、法人與信託', 'Identity information: individuals, legal persons and trusts', [
    block('收集與核實須分開', 'Distinguish collection from verification', [
        ('對自然人，至少要收集全名、出生日期、國籍、獨特識別號碼及文件類別；核實的則是全名、出生日期、號碼及文件類別。第4.3.3段的例子是：(a) 香港身份證或其他國家的身份證；(b) 有效的旅遊證件（例如未過期的護照）；或 (c) 其他可靠及獨立來源所提供的相關文件、數據或資料（例如政府機構發出的文件）。還須取得居住地址資料，但這並不表示每個客戶都一律要另交一份地址證明。', 'For individuals, collect at least full name, date of birth, nationality, unique identification number and document type; verify the name, date of birth, number and document type. Paragraph 4.3.3 gives these examples: (a) a Hong Kong identity card or other national identity card; (b) a valid travel document (for example an unexpired passport); or (c) other relevant documents, data or information from a reliable and independent source (for example a document issued by a government body). Also obtain residential-address information; this does not impose a universal requirement for a separate address-proof document.'),
        ('對法人，至少要收集全名、成立、註冊或登記的日期及地點（包括註冊辦事處地址）、識別號碼及文件類別，以及在不同於註冊地址時的主要營業地點。核實的是名稱、法律形式、當時仍然存在，以及規管或約束其權力的安排。', 'For legal persons, collect at least the full name, the date and place of incorporation, establishment or registration (including the registered office), the identification number and document type, and the principal place of business if it is different from the registered address. Verify the name, legal form, current existence, and the powers that govern or bind the legal person.'),
        ('核實法人時，可用的來源例子有八類，見指引第4.3.7段：(a) 公司註冊證明書；(b) 獨立公司註冊登記冊的記錄；(c) 職權證明書；(d) 良好聲譽證明書；(e) 註冊記錄；(f) 合夥協議或契約；(g) 章程文件；或 (h) 其他可靠及獨立來源所提供的相關文件、數據或資料（例如政府機構發出的文件）。通常，成立證明只證明名稱及法律形式，未必證明現時仍然存在，因此可能需要多於一份文件。', 'When verifying a legal person, eight example sources are listed in paragraph 4.3.7: (a) a certificate of incorporation; (b) a record in an independent company registry; (c) a certificate of incumbency; (d) a certificate of good standing; (e) a record of registration; (f) a partnership agreement or deed; (g) a constitutional document; or (h) other relevant documents, data or information from a reliable and independent source (for example a document issued by a government body). An incorporation certificate alone may prove only the name and legal form, and may not prove current existence, so more than one document may be needed.'),
        ('對信託或類似法律安排，收集的最低資料與核實項目也不完全相同。至少須收集名稱、成立或設立日期、管限法律的司法管轄區、官方識別號碼及文件類別（如有），以及註冊辦事處地址（如適用）。核實名稱、形式、現時存在及約束權力時，可用信託契據、適當登記冊，或指定專業確認。', 'For a trust or similar legal arrangement, the minimum information to be collected is not identical to the items that must be verified. For trusts/similar arrangements collect the name, the date of establishment or settlement, the governing jurisdiction, any official identification number and document type, and the registered office if applicable. Verify the name, form, current existence and binding powers using a deed, a suitable register, or a specified professional confirmation.'),
        ('如果受託人代表一個沒有獨立法人地位的信託，去建立關係或進行交易，該受託人通常本身也是客戶，須按其是自然人或法人的身分，依相應要求進行審查。', 'Where a trustee acts for a trust that has no separate legal personality, in establishing a relationship or carrying out a transaction, the trustee is generally also the customer, and must be checked under the relevant individual or legal-person requirements.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.3.2–4.3.13段及註18–20', '¶4.3.2–4.3.13; footnotes 18–20', 'cannot act as a proof of current existence'),
    ], kind='comparison'),
    block('文件可靠性及關連人士', 'Document reliability and connected parties', [
        ('用來核實的資料，在提供或取得時必須仍然有效，並按風險採取防偽措施。在場客戶的一般做法，是查閱正本並保留副本；客戶不能提供正本時，須另外確保資料可靠。如果資料是外文，還須採取適當步驟，確認它確能證明身分。', 'Verification information must still be current when it is supplied or obtained, and risk-based anti-fraud measures should be applied. Generally sight originals and keep copies for customers who are physically present; where originals cannot be provided, reliability must be ensured in another way. If the identity evidence is in a foreign language, take suitable steps to confirm that it does in fact prove identity.'),
        ('身分文件應有照片。只有在確有例外，而且相關風險已經妥善評估及緩減的情況下，才可以接受沒有照片的文件。', 'Identity documents should contain a photograph. A document without a photograph is acceptable only exceptionally, and only where the associated risks have been properly assessed and mitigated.'),
        ('對關連人士，須取得其姓名：公司董事、合夥人、信託受託人；其他情況則是高級管理層，或具執行權力的自然人。如果這個人同時是客戶、實益擁有人或代表，便須按較適用的要求去識別及核實，不能只記下一個姓名。', 'Obtain the names of connected parties: directors, partners and trustees, or otherwise senior or executive natural persons. If the same person is also the customer, a beneficial owner or a representative, apply the corresponding identification and verification duties; collecting only a name is not enough.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.3.4、4.3.14–4.3.19段及註26', '¶4.3.4, 4.3.14–4.3.19; footnotes 26', 'identify all the connected parties'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('常見文件情況', 'Common documentary situations', [
        ('旅行證件一般只須保留個人資料頁。如果姓名有改變，須用新文件核實，並與原有出生日期、識別號碼等核對。主要營業地址是指實際的主要營運地點，如果與資料不一致，便須查詢。可靠獨立文件已載有註冊地址，而且並不知道該地址已過期，便可接受作為地址資料。', 'Generally retain the biodata page of a travel document. If the name has changed, verify it with new evidence and corroborate the date of birth and identifier. The principal business address is the actual main operating location; enquire into any inconsistency. A reliable independent document may be used as evidence of a registered address, unless it is known to be outdated.'),
        ('合夥可以用登記紀錄，或合夥協議、契據來核實。非高風險情況，可用適當的摘錄或刪節版；但登記紀錄未必載有規管權力，因此可能還需要額外文件。對於具有悠久歷史、良好聲譽，而且有大量公開的合伙人及控制人資料的知名機構，在所述條件下，可用專業或行業會員確認。', 'A partnership can be verified using a registration record, or a partnership agreement or deed. In a case that is not high-risk, an appropriate extract or redacted version may be used. Registration may not show the governing powers, so another document may still be needed. For a well-known, reputable organisation with a long history and substantial public information about its partners or controllers, confirmation of professional or trade membership may suffice under the stated conditions.'),
        ('了解擁有權及控制結構是必須的，但這不表示每一次都要索取擁有權圖，也不表示必須例行核實每一層中間公司的全部資料。應按結構的複雜性、風險，以及現有資料是否足以識別實益擁有人，來決定要取多少。', 'Understanding the ownership and control structure is mandatory. That does not mean an ownership chart must be obtained every time, or that every intermediate company must routinely be verified in full. Decide by complexity, risk, and whether the information is sufficient to identify the beneficial owners.'),
        ('可靠來源的電子正本可以使用。客戶自行提供的列印本，可能要與登記冊等核對；機構直接從可靠來源下載的，便不必再做同一項核對。翻譯必須可靠、適當，但不一定必須由專業第三方提供。舊文件日後到期，並不會自動要求重新核實，但仍須維持CDD資料更新。', 'Reliable electronic originals may be used. A printout supplied by the customer may need to be corroborated against a registry or similar source, whereas a direct download by the MSO from a reliable source need not repeat that same check. A translation must be appropriate and reliable, but it does not have to come from a professional third party. Later expiry of an old document does not, by itself, automatically require re-verification; CDD information must still be kept current.'),
    ], [
        ref('06', '打擊洗錢問答A3–A8、A13–A15', 'AML/CFT FAQ A3–A8, A13–A15', 'biodata'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('國籍核實、地址及更名的條件', 'Nationality verification, addresses and name-change conditions', [
        ('自然人的最低識別資料包括國籍，但「取得」和「核實」不是同一件事。第4.3.3段的一般核實項目，是姓名、出生日期、唯一識別號碼及證件類型，並不是一律要另行核實國籍。不能因此便略去應取得的國籍資料。例如：職員已從身分證抄下國籍，並核實了姓名、出生日期、證件號碼及類型，通常便已符合這項一般核實範圍；但不能因為國籍不是獨立核實項目，便完全不收集國籍。', 'Minimum identification information for an individual includes nationality, but collecting a fact and verifying it are not the same task. The general verification set in paragraph 4.3.3 is name, date of birth, unique identifier and document type; nationality is not universally a separate verification item. Nationality must still be obtained. For example: copying nationality from an identity card, and verifying name, date of birth, document number and type, will usually meet this general verification set. That is not a reason to skip collecting nationality altogether.'),
        ('須取得居住地址資料，但不代表每個客戶都一律要交獨立的地址證明。如果客戶在建立關係前已經更名，只需識別及核實現用姓名。如果是在關係建立之後才更名，則須核實新姓名，並與既有的出生日期、證件號碼核對；有疑問時，可要求結婚證明或改名契。', 'Obtain residential-address information, without imposing a universal requirement for a separate address-proof document. If the name changed before the relationship began, identify and verify only the current name. If the name changes after the relationship has been established, verify the new name and corroborate it against the existing date of birth and document number; if there is doubt, a marriage certificate or a deed poll may be requested.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.3.2–4.3.5、4.3.13段及註17–18', '¶4.3.2–4.3.5, 4.3.13; footnotes 17–18', 'nationality'),
        ref('06', '打擊洗錢問答A4', 'AML/CFT FAQ A4', 'only the current name'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('信託核實的五類來源與組織合法目的', 'Five trust-verification sources and legitimate organisational purpose', [
        ('核實信託時，要核對的是名稱、法律形式、現時是否存在，以及規管或約束其權力的安排。可參照的例子有五類：(1) 信託契據或類似文書；(2) 成立地的適當登記冊；(3) 以專業身分行事的受託人書面確認；(4) 已審閱有關文書的律師書面確認；(5) 與金錢服務經營者同一金融集團的信託公司書面確認，但須由該公司管理該信託。', 'When verifying a trust, the points to check are its name, legal form, current existence, and the arrangements that regulate or bind its powers. To verify a trust’s name, legal form, current existence and regulating/binding powers, examples are (1) a deed or similar instrument; (2) an appropriate register in its country of establishment; (3) written confirmation from a professional trustee; (4) written confirmation from a lawyer who has reviewed the instrument; or (5) confirmation from a trust company in the same financial group as the MSO, but only where that company manages the trust.'),
        ('特殊情況可以保留遮蓋了部分內容的契據副本。所謂適當登記冊，須有足夠透明度，並保持擁有及控制資料更新。專業受託人的業務包括信託管理或行政服務，並不是任何自稱受託人的個人，都符合這一項替代來源。', 'A redacted copy of a deed may exceptionally be retained. An appropriate register needs adequate transparency, and current ownership and control information. A professional trustee provides trust administration or management services in a profession or business; not every self-described trustee qualifies for that alternative.'),
        ('協會、會所、社團、慈善團體、宗教組織、學會、互助或友愛社團、合作或公積社團等，另須信納其目的是合法的，例如可以查閱章程。只核實註冊資料，並不能取代這項對目的的了解。', 'For associations, clubs, societies, charities, religious bodies, institutes, mutual or friendly societies, and cooperative or provident societies, also satisfy yourself as to legitimate purpose, for example by sighting the constitution. Registration checks do not replace this enquiry into purpose.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.3.9、4.3.12段及註23–25', '¶4.3.9, 4.3.12; footnotes 23–25', 'written confirmation from a trust company which is within the same financial group'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('identity-evidence', '身分文件與核證副本', 'Identity documents and certified copies', [
    block('常用文件與例外', 'Documents and exceptions', [
        ('用來核實個人身分的文件，要先分清這個人是否香港居民，以及當時是否身在香港。附錄A第1段先處理身在香港的個人，然後再特別規定：香港居民「應經常」以香港身分證或簽證身分書識別及核實，英文為 should always。依既定裁決，學習時須同時記住兩語措辭，實務上以香港身分證或簽證身分書處理香港居民；這項居民規則，不只限於親身在港的人。非居民如果親身在香港，則使用有效旅行證件。', 'The document used to verify an individual depends on whether the person is a Hong Kong resident, and on whether the person is in Hong Kong at the time. Appendix A paragraph 1 first addresses individuals present in Hong Kong, then specifically says Hong Kong residents should always be identified and verified using a Hong Kong identity card or a document of identity. The Chinese text says 「應經常」 (usually). Retain the language difference under the settled decision, and in practice use an HKID or document of identity for Hong Kong residents; the resident rule is not confined to physical presence in Hong Kong. A non-resident who is present in Hong Kong uses a valid travel document.'),
        ('如果非居民並沒有親身在香港，可用的文件範圍便不同。應使用有效護照或其他旅行證件、附有照片的國民身分證，或由主管國家或政府機構簽發、附有照片的有效國民駕駛執照。國際駕駛許可證或執照不獲接受；也不應把這個境外非居民的文件清單，套用到所有客戶身上。', 'A different document list applies where the person is a non-resident and is not physically present in Hong Kong. For non-residents not physically present in Hong Kong, use a valid passport or other travel document, a photo national identity card, or a valid photo national driving licence issued by a competent national or government agency. International driving permits or licences are not acceptable, and this remote non-resident list must not be applied indiscriminately to every customer.'),
        ('「旅行證件」的範圍，比護照更廣。指引列出的還包括澳門永久性居民身分證、台灣居民來往大陸通行證、海員身分證、往來台灣通行證、澳門居民入境許可證、因公往來港澳通行證，以及往來港澳通行證。', 'A “travel document” is a wider category than a passport. Travel documents are not limited to passports: the list includes Macau permanent resident identity cards, the Mainland Travel Permit for Taiwan Residents, a Seaman’s Identity Document, the Taiwan Travel Permit for Mainland Residents, permits for Macau residents, and official-purpose or ordinary exit-entry permits for Hong Kong and Macau.'),
        ('未成年人如果在香港出生，又沒有有效的旅行證件或身分證，可用香港出生證明核實，並同時記錄及核實代表或陪同的父母或監護人身分。在沒有國民身分證制度，而且客戶沒有附照片旅行證件或駕照的地區，可在例外情況及風險為本方法下接受其他證據，並盡量使用有照片的文件。', 'A different route is available for some children. For a Hong Kong-born minor without a valid travel document/ID, verify using the birth certificate and record and verify the representing or accompanying parent or guardian. In a jurisdiction without a national identity-card system, where the customer also lacks a photo travel document or driving licence, other evidence may exceptionally be accepted under a risk-based approach, preferably with a photograph.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '附錄A第1–6段及註72–73', 'Appendix A ¶1–6, footnotes 72–73', 'international drivers permits and licences are not acceptable'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('核證程序及責任', 'Certification and responsibility', [
        ('如果使用核證副本，核證者必須獨立、適當，而且曾經親眼看過正本。例子包括合資格中介人、對等司法管轄區的司法人員、證件發出國的使領館人員、太平紳士，以及會計師、律師、公證人或特許秘書等專業人士。', 'Where a certified copy is used, the certifier must be independent and appropriate, and must have seen the original. Examples include eligible intermediaries, members of the judiciary in an equivalent jurisdiction, embassy or consulate officials of the issuing country, Justices of the Peace, and professionals such as accountants, lawyers, notaries and chartered secretaries.'),
        ('核證副本須有簽署及日期，清晰列出姓名及職銜或身分，並聲明與正本相符。一般而言，由客戶自行核證是不足夠的；但法人客戶內部、受專業操守約束的專業人士，以其專業身分核證，可以作為例外。', 'The certified copy needs a signature and date, a clearly stated name and position or capacity, and a statement that it is a true copy. Customer self-certification is generally insufficient. A professional within a legal-person customer may, exceptionally, qualify if that person is bound by professional conduct rules and is acting in a professional capacity.'),
        ('接受核證副本，並不會把客戶盡職審查的責任轉走。對來自高風險地區的核證副本，或對來自任何地區、不受規管的實體所核證的副本，須特別審慎。如果不能確定真確性，或懷疑文件並非關乎該客戶，便應採取額外的風險緩減措施。', 'Accepting certified copies does not transfer CDD responsibility away from the MSO. Exercise particular care with copies from higher-risk countries, or with copies certified by unregulated entities in any jurisdiction. If authenticity is uncertain, or the document may not relate to the customer, additional risk-mitigation measures should be taken.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '附錄A第7–10段及註74–76', 'Appendix A ¶7–10, footnotes 74–76', 'the certifier will need to have seen the original'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('查冊、核證與地址要求的補充', 'Company searches, certification and address requirements', [
        ('公司註冊證書本身，並不能證明該公司現時仍然存在；如果採用公司登記查冊，應取得完整的公司查冊報告。核證人除了簽署、日期、身分，以及「與正本相符」的聲明之外，還應在簽署下方以大寫清晰列印姓名。', 'A certificate of incorporation alone does not prove that the company currently exists. Where verification is done through a company registry, a full company search report should be obtained. In addition to the signature, date, capacity and true-copy statement, the certifier should clearly print the name in capitals below the signature.'),
        ('文件03的附錄A，還有一些用來辨認證件的說明，包括：香港居民年滿11歲須登記領取身分證，以及永久居民身分證在出生日期下方的「A」字標記。這些只是本版附錄裡的辨認細節，不能把單一標記當成整套身分核實程序。', 'Document 03 Appendix A also includes recognition details, including Hong Kong resident registration for an identity card from the age of 11, and the “A” marker beneath the date of birth on permanent Hong Kong identity cards. These are recognition details in this edition of the Appendix, not a substitute for complete identity verification.'),
        ('指引並不一律要求核實居住地址；集團政策，或其他本地或境外的法律、監管要求，則可能需要核實。如果機構要求核實地址，應向客戶清楚解釋原因，不能把機構自己的額外要求，說成是指引對所有客戶的統一規定。', 'The Guideline does not universally require verification of a residential address, although group policy or other local or overseas legal or regulatory requirements may do so. If address verification is required, clearly explain the reasons to the customer, and distinguish those additional institutional requirements from a universal requirement in the Guideline.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.3.5段及註18', '¶4.3.5; footnotes 18', 'communicate clearly to the customer the reasons'),
        ref('03', '附錄A第4–5、9段及註73、76', 'Appendix A ¶4–5, 9; footnotes 73, 76', 'obtaining a full company search'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('beneficial-owners', '實益擁有人：擁有權、控制與代他人行事', 'Beneficial owners: ownership, control and acting for another', [
    block('定義及控制標準', 'Definitions and control tests', [
        ('實益擁有人（beneficial owner）和發牌裡的「最終擁有人」（ultimate owner）不是同一個概念。實益擁有人是最終擁有或控制該客戶的人，或者是該筆交易代其進行的人。自然人客戶通常本身就是自己的實益擁有人；但如果有跡象顯示這個人並不是為自己行事，便須作適當查詢。例如：顧客看起來像是為自己兌換，但其實是依照另一個人的指示，把錢交給那個人，便可能要進一步查這筆交易是代誰進行。', 'A beneficial owner is not the same concept as an “ultimate owner” in the licensing sense. A beneficial owner ultimately owns/controls the customer, or is the person on whose behalf the transaction is conducted. An individual customer is normally its own beneficial owner, but indications that the person is not acting for himself or herself require enquiries. For example: a customer who appears to be exchanging money for personal use, but who is in fact acting on another person’s instructions and handing the proceeds to that person, may need further enquiry into the person on whose behalf the transaction is conducted.'),
        ('公司客戶的實益擁有人，包括直接或間接擁有或控制超過25%股本的自然人、可行使或控制超過25%表決權的自然人，或最終控制管理層的自然人；如果公司是代別人行事，該人亦包括在內。超過25%包括25.1%及25.5%，不是到26%才符合。恰好25%單獨並不符合這個比例條件，但仍可能因為最終管理控制等另一準則而符合。例如：某人剛好持有25%股份，而且沒有其他控制權，便不是因為持股而成為實益擁有人；如果同一人可以最終決定管理層，則仍可能按控制準則被識別。', 'For a corporate customer, the beneficial owners include individuals who directly or indirectly own or control more than 25% of the capital, or who can exercise or control more than 25% of the voting rights, or who exercise ultimate management control; also the person for whom it acts. More than 25% includes 25.1% and 25.5%; the threshold is not 26%. Exactly 25% does not, by itself, satisfy the percentage test, but another control test may still apply. For example: a person who holds exactly 25% of the shares and has no other control is not a beneficial owner by reason of that shareholding alone; the same person may still have to be identified if that person can ultimately decide management.'),
        ('合夥的實益擁有人，是擁有超過25%資本、利潤或表決權的自然人，或最終控制管理的自然人。對於不是合夥的其他非法團組織，則是最終擁有或控制的自然人，以及該組織代其行事的其他人。', 'For a partnership, the beneficial owners are individuals with more than 25% of the capital, profits or voting rights, or with ultimate management control. For other unincorporated bodies that are not partnerships, they are the individuals who ultimately own or control the body, and the persons for whom the body acts.'),
        ('信託的實益擁有人範圍，不能只看成「持股超過25%的人」。對信託財產有既得權益的受益人或受益人類別、財產授予人、受託人、保護人或執行人，以及最終控制的自然人，都要按定義識別。如果受益人是按特徵或類別指定的，須有足夠資料，以便在支付或行使既得權利時，能夠確定其身分。', 'The beneficial owners of a trust are not simply “anyone who owns more than 25%”. For trusts: vested-interest beneficiaries or classes, the settlor, the trustee, the protector or enforcer, and individuals with ultimate control, must all be identified under their definitions. Where beneficiaries are designated by characteristics or class, obtain enough information to establish identity at the time of payout or of the exercise of vested rights.'),
        ('如果法人客戶沒有任何自然人符合實益擁有人的定義，須識別高級管理人員，並採取合理措施核實其身分。不能只因為沒有人持股超過25%，便立即停止追查控制權。識別這些高級管理人員，是在沒有符合定義的實益擁有人時的替代步驟，並不是把他們自動重新定義為實益擁有人。', 'If no natural person meets the beneficial-owner definition for a legal-person customer, identify the senior managing officials and take reasonable measures to verify their identity. The mere absence of a shareholder above 25% does not, by itself, end the search for control. Identifying those officials is a fallback where no one meets the definition; it does not automatically redefine them as beneficial owners.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.4.1–4.4.12段', '¶4.4.1–4.4.12', 'more than 25% of the issued share capital'),
    ], kind='comparison'),
    block('核實及特殊結構', 'Verification and special structures', [
        ('核實實益擁有人，須採取合理措施，而且程度要按客戶及關係的風險來調整。可以把可靠的公開資料、客戶提供的獨立文件，以及聲明互相核對。如果架構複雜，須了解每一層及其合理理由，不能只停在中間的公司。', 'Take reasonable measures to verify beneficial owners, and make the intensity risk-sensitive to the customer and the relationship. Public information, independent documents and customer declarations can be corroborated against one another. For a complex structure, understand the intermediate layers and the legitimate reasons for them; do not stop at an intermediate company.'),
        ('如果公司有不記名股票，而這些股票由合資格保管人持有，須取得獨立證據，以及保管人和權益人的身分，並定期確認。否則，須在開戶前及其後每年，取得各實益擁有人的聲明，並要求一旦持有權有變更，便須即時通知。代名股東同樣要查出其代表的人，以及有關安排。', 'Where bearer shares are held by an authorised or registered custodian, obtain independent evidence and the identities of the custodian and the entitled persons, and confirm these periodically. Otherwise, obtain owner declarations before the account is opened and annually thereafter, and require immediate notification of any change in holdings. Nominee shareholders must also be identified, together with their principals and the arrangements.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.4.3–4.4.4、4.4.13–4.4.18段', '¶4.4.3–4.4.4, 4.4.13–4.4.18', 'annually thereafter from each beneficial owner'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('實益擁有人資料與極低風險核實', 'BO information and exceptionally-low-risk verification', [
        ('實益擁有人的識別資料，應盡量設法取得與自然人客戶相同的項目：姓名、出生日期、國籍、唯一識別號碼及證件類型。核實須合理，並按風險進行，可以參照公開紀錄、可靠獨立資料，或核對客戶聲明。「盡量取得」這些資料，並不等於一律可以免去核實。', 'Endeavour, as far as possible, to obtain the same identification information for a beneficial owner as for an individual customer: name, date of birth, nationality, unique identifier and document type. Verification must be reasonable and risk-sensitive, and may use public records, reliable independent evidence, or corroborated customer declarations. Endeavouring to obtain the information is not a general waiver of verification.'),
        ('在極低風險的情況，例如慈善信託，可能合理地用客戶提供的資料（包括已核實身分的受託人），以及確認該客戶認識該實益擁有人，來確認身分。必須先有相應的極低風險判斷，不是所有慈善組織都可以自動豁免。', 'In an exceptionally low-risk situation, such as a charitable trust, it may be reasonable to confirm identity using information from the customer, including verified trustees, together with confirmation that the beneficial owner is known to the customer. This needs the exceptionally-low-risk context; it is not an automatic exemption for every charity.'),
        ('不記名認股權證，是一種實體證書，持有人可以憑它取得法人的擁有權，並且可以轉讓。對不記名股票所採取的保管、聲明等管控，同樣適用於這類權證，以及其他沒有可追查性的類似文書。', 'A bearer-share warrant is a negotiable physical certificate that entitles its holder to ownership in a legal person. The custody and declaration controls that apply to bearer shares also apply to those warrants, and to similar untraceable instruments.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.4.2–4.4.3、4.4.15–4.4.17段及註30', '¶4.4.2–4.4.3, 4.4.15–4.4.17; footnotes 30', 'The same controls should be applied to bearer share warrants'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('自然人與「人」的界線', 'Individuals versus “persons”', [
        ('公司或合夥的擁有權及控制分支，追查的是自然人。但是，交易代其進行的人，以及信託裡的財產授予人、受託人、保障人或執行人等角色，須按各自的定義識別，不能一律把法人排除在外。', 'The ownership and control tests do not all work in the same way. Ownership/control limbs for corporations and partnerships trace individuals. But the person for whom a transaction is conducted, and trust roles such as settlor, trustee and protector or enforcer, must be identified under their respective definitions; legal persons are not universally excluded.'),
    ], [
        ref('04', '附表2第1條', 'Schedule 2 s.1', 'beneficial owner'),
        ref('03', '第4.4.6–4.4.12段', '¶4.4.6–4.4.12', 'senior managing official'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('認識：重要控制人登記冊及CDD的關係', 'Recognise: the significant controllers register and CDD', [
        ('海關指引註27說明，公司須備存實益擁有人登記冊，例如按香港《公司條例》備存的重要控制人登記冊。金錢服務經營者可以參閱這類登記冊，協助識別實益擁有人；如果資料並不公開，可以直接向客戶索取紀錄。即使取得了登記冊，仍須按本節核實，並了解擁有權及控制結構，不能把取得登記冊當成已經完成全部客戶盡職審查。', 'Guideline note 27 records that companies are required to maintain registers of their beneficial owners, for example the significant controllers register under the Companies Ordinance of Hong Kong. An MSO may refer to such registers to assist identification of beneficial owners; where a register is not publicly available, the MSO may obtain the record directly from the customer. The verification and the ownership and control analysis in this section still apply; obtaining the register is not completion of all CDD.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.4.3–4.4.4段及註27', '¶4.4.3–4.4.4 and note 27', 'An MSO may refer to such registers'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('理解：沒有持股也可有最終控制權', 'Understand: ultimate control without share ownership', [
        ('常見問題解答所舉的例子包括：透過與持股或表決權超過25%的擁有人之間的私人關連來施加控制；或者藉參與企業融資、密切家庭關係、歷史或合約聯繫，或公司違反某些付款約定，而取得控制。這些只是可能構成控制的例子，不是把所有親屬、債權人或合約對手，都自動當成實益擁有人。', 'FAQ examples include control through personal connections to owners of more than 25% of the shares or voting rights, or through enterprise financing, close family relationships, historical or contractual associations, or a company’s default on particular payments. These are possible routes to control, not automatic beneficial-owner status for every relative, creditor or contracting party.'),
        ('即使控制權從未實際行使，也可能從使用、享受或得益於法人資產等情況，推定控制仍然存在。相反，如果在客戶盡職審查過程中取得的資料，完全沒有顯示另有最終控制人，常見問題解答並不要求積極再去尋找這樣一個人。這並不免除已知擁有權、控制結構，以及其他實益擁有人分支的識別要求。', 'Control may be presumed even if it has never actually been exercised, for example through using, enjoying or benefiting from the legal person’s assets. Conversely, where nothing obtained during CDD suggests that another ultimate controller exists, the FAQ does not require the MSO to go out and actively identify such a person. This does not waive identification under known ownership or control structures, or under the other beneficial-owner limbs.'),
    ], [
        ref('06', '打擊洗錢問答A10（比例按法例及指引統一為超過25%）', 'AML/CFT FAQ A10 (percentage follows the law/Guideline: more than 25%)', 'exerts control without ownership'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('representatives', '代表客戶行事者與授權', 'Persons acting for customers and authorisation', [
    block('PPTA的身分及權力', 'PPTA identity and authority', [
        ('誰是代表客戶行事的人（PPTA），要按角色、獲授權的活動及風險來判定，包括代表建立關係的人，或獲授權發指示的人。須有清晰的政策，並且一致執行。法人客戶一般至少會有一位代表建立關係的人。', 'Who counts as a person acting for the customer (a PPTA) is determined by roles, authorised activities and risk. This includes persons who establish the relationship, or who are authorised to give instructions. Apply clear, consistent policies. A legal-person customer generally has at least one representative who establishes the relationship.'),
        ('代表的身分，和授權，要分開處理。須按自然人或法人的相應要求，取得並核實代表的身分，並另外用適當文件核實每位代表的權力，例如董事會決議或類似的書面授權。只取名片，或只聽對方口頭說自己獲授權，都不能代替驗證授權。', 'A representative’s identity and authority must be dealt with separately. Apply relevant individual/legal-person identification and verification requirements, and separately verify each representative’s authority using appropriate evidence, such as a board resolution or equivalent written authorisation. A business card, or a mere assertion that the person is authorised, does not establish authority.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.5.1–4.5.4段', '¶4.5.1–4.5.4', 'verify the authority of each PPTA'),
        ref('07', '附錄第(3)部分', 'Appendix (3)', 'at least one PPTA'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('獲授權代表及低風險核實', 'Authorized representatives and low-risk verification', [
        ('公司可以由已經核實授權的僱員，親身建立關係，並不要求每名董事或實益擁有人都親自到場。一個人被列為授權簽署人，只有在實際代表客戶行事的範圍內，才須按代表客戶行事的人（PPTA）的要求處理。', 'A properly authorized employee may establish a corporate relationship in person; every director or beneficial owner need not attend personally. An authorized signatory requires PPTA treatment when that person acts for the customer.'),
        ('在低風險關係，代表人名單可以用來支持合理核實，但有條件：名單內的身分及授權，須由客戶內部、獨立於這些代表人的部門或人士確認，例如合規、審核或人力資源部門。仍須取得每名代表適用的基本識別資料，不能只保存一份未經確認的姓名表。', 'A name list is not automatically enough, even in a lower-risk case. For low-risk relationships a representative list may support reasonable verification where identity and authority are confirmed by a department or person within the customer who is independent of those representatives, such as compliance, audit or human resources. Obtain the applicable basic identity details for every PPTA; an unconfirmed name list is not sufficient.'),
    ], [
        ref('06', '打擊洗錢問答A9、A11–A12', 'AML/CFT FAQ A9, A11–A12', 'appropriate measures which are commensurate with the ML/TF risks'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('記憶：PPTA最低識別資料的四項與五項', 'Remember: four and five minimum PPTA identification items', [
        ('自然人代表至少要取得四項識別資料：(1) 全名；(2) 出生日期；(3) 國籍；(4) 獨特識別號碼及文件類別。文件類別與號碼是合列為一項的；不能只記姓名及證件號碼，卻省略出生日期或國籍。', 'For an individual PPTA, obtain at least four identification items: (1) full name; (2) date of birth; (3) nationality; and (4) unique identification number and document type. The number and the type form one listed item. Recording only a name and an identity-document number omits date of birth and nationality.'),
        ('法人代表至少要取得五項識別資料：(1) 全名；(2) 註冊、成立或登記日期；(3) 註冊、成立或登記地點，包括註冊辦事處地址；(4) 獨特識別號碼及文件類別；(5) 主要營業地點（如與註冊辦事處地址不同）。這只是識別資料清單；合理核實身分，以及另外核實授權的責任，仍然要履行。', 'For a legal-person PPTA, obtain at least five identification items: (1) full name; (2) date of incorporation, establishment or registration; (3) place of incorporation, establishment or registration, including the registered-office address; (4) unique identification number and document type; and (5) the principal place of business, if different from the registered office. These are identification data only; reasonable identity verification, and separate verification of authority, remain required.'),
        ('法人如果透過面對面渠道開戶，至少應有一名獲授權建立關係的自然人現身；不需要所有董事或實益擁有人都到場。如果代表法人開戶的人，沒有親身在場接受識別，便須按非面對面風險來處理，例如採取額外的客戶盡職審查，或使用關長認可、而且屬可靠獨立來源的數碼識別系統。不能因為法人本身不可能現身，便忽略代表所用渠道的風險。', 'Where a legal person opens through a face-to-face channel, at least one natural person authorized to establish the relationship should be physically present; all directors or beneficial owners need not attend. If the person acting for the legal person is not present for identification, mitigate the non-face-to-face risks, for example with additional CDD, or with a reliable independent digital identification system recognized by the CCE. The fact that a legal person cannot attend in person does not remove the channel risk attached to its representative.'),
    ], [
        ref('06', '打擊洗錢問答A9、A12', 'AML/CFT FAQ A9, A12', 'Natural person PPTA'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('timing', '核實時間、延後條件及審查失敗', 'Verification timing, deferral and failed CDD', [
    block('一般規則與有限延後', 'General rule and limited deferral', [
        ('客戶盡職審查有時間要求：必須先完成所需審查，才能建立關係，或執行已達門檻的非經常交易。「建立關係後才延後核實身分」這項例外，並不適用於非經常交易。例如：一筆沒有業務關係、已達港幣120,000元的兌換，不能先做交易，再補做身分核實。', 'CDD has a timing rule. Complete required CDD before establishing a relationship, or before carrying out a threshold occasional transaction. The exception that allows identity verification to be deferred until after a relationship has been established does not apply to occasional transactions. For example: a one-off exchange of at least HK$120,000, with no business relationship, cannot be carried out first and have identity verification completed later.'),
        ('只有在建立業務關係時，身分核實才可以例外延後，而且三個條件必須同時符合：由此帶來的風險得到有效管理；延後是為了避免妨礙正常業務而有必要；以及在合理切實可行的範圍內盡快完成核實。', 'Deferral is a narrow exception, not a regular practice, and it is available only when establishing a business relationship. Identity verification may exceptionally follow relationship establishment only if all of the following are met: the resulting risk is effectively managed; deferral is necessary so as not to interrupt normal business; and verification is completed as soon as reasonably practicable.'),
        ('即使獲准延後核實，仍須設下合理的完成期限，並且為逾期個案作跟進；同時限制交易的數目、種類或金額，監察異常的大額或複雜交易，並定期向管理層報告尚未完成的個案。在這段期間，一般不得向第三方付款。', 'Even where verification is deferred, set a reasonable deadline and follow up overdue cases. Also limit the number, type or amount of transactions, monitor large or complex abnormal activity, and report pending cases to management periodically. Generally do not make payments to third parties during this period.'),
        ('在延後核實期間，向第三方付款只可以作為例外，而且四個條件必須一併符合：沒有懷疑；風險評為低；獲高級管理層按客戶的業務性質批准；以及受款人不在恐怖分子、政治人物等監察名單上。缺任何一項，都不應在此期間向第三方付款。', 'A third-party payment during deferred verification is exceptional, and all four conditions must be met: there is no suspicion; the risk is assessed as low; senior management has given approval having regard to the customer’s business; and the recipient’s name does not match watchlists such as terrorist or PEP lists. If any one of these is missing, a third-party payment should not be made during the deferral period.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.7.1–4.7.3段', '¶4.7.1–4.7.3', 'necessary not to interrupt the normal conduct'),
        ref('04', '附表2第3條', 'Schedule 2 s.3', 'before carrying out for the customer an occasional transaction'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('不能完成CDD的後果', 'Consequences of inability to complete CDD', [
        ('如果不能完成客戶盡職審查，便不得建立關係，也不得執行非經常交易；已經建立的關係，須在合理切實可行的範圍內盡快終止。如果未能在合理的核實期限內完成，便須停止進一步交易，只有在盡可能按原形式退回資金或資產時，才屬例外。', 'If the required CDD cannot be completed, do not establish the relationship and do not execute an occasional transaction. If a relationship has already been established, terminate it as soon as reasonably practicable. If a reasonable verification deadline is missed, stop further transactions, except for returning funds or assets in their original form as far as possible.'),
        ('還要評估這次失敗，是否已經形成知悉或懷疑，並在適當時向聯合財富情報組（JFIU）舉報；尤其要留意沒有合理理由便要求轉至第三方，或把現金轉換形式的情況。不得開立或維持匿名或虛構姓名的戶口。編號戶口見下一段。', 'Also assess whether the failure itself creates knowledge or suspicion, and report to the Joint Financial Intelligence Unit (JFIU) where appropriate, especially where there is no reasonable explanation for a transfer to a third party, or for a change in the form of cash. Anonymous or fictitious-name accounts must not be opened or maintained. Numbered accounts are dealt with next.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.7.4、4.13.1–4.14.1段', '¶4.7.4, 4.13.1–4.14.1', 'must not open, or maintain any anonymous account'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('號碼戶口仍須在付款訊息使用真名', 'Numbered accounts still use real names in payment messages', [
        ('編號戶口不能用來迴避完整的客戶盡職審查。合規、審核及其他獲授權員工須可取得有關資料，並且須有足夠員工知道持有人的身分。所有電傳或匯款訊息，都必須反映戶口持有人的真實姓名，不能只填一個號碼來隱藏身分。例如：內部用「戶口017」來稱呼客戶，對外的付款訊息仍須寫上持有人的真名，而不是只寫017。', 'A numbered account does not avoid full CDD. Compliance, audit and other authorized staff need access to the information, and sufficient staff must know the holder’s identity. All wire or remittance messages must reflect the real account-holder name, and must not conceal identity behind a number. For example: even if the customer is known internally as “account 017”, the outward payment message must still carry the holder’s real name, not only the number 017.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.14.1段及註50', '¶4.14.1; footnotes 50', 'must reflect the real name of the account holder'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('simplified', '簡化盡職審查：可減甚麼、不能免甚麼', 'Simplified due diligence: permitted reductions and limits', [
    block('低風險簡化與法定實益擁有人例外', 'Low-risk simplification and beneficial-owner exceptions', [
        ('簡化盡職審查（SDD）不是「低風險便甚麼都不用做」。必須先有充分的風險分析，支持低風險這個判斷，而且簡化的程度要與風險相稱。例如可以降低資料更新或交易監察的頻率，或者由交易或關係的類型來推斷目的及性質。即使如此，仍須持續監察。', 'Simplified due diligence (SDD) is not a licence to skip all checks simply because the risk is low. A low-risk finding must be supported by adequate analysis, and any simplification must be proportionate to the risk. Examples include less frequent updates or monitoring, or inferring purpose and nature from the type of transaction or relationship. Ongoing monitoring remains required.'),
        ('簡化審查一旦不再符合條件，便必須停下。如果風險已經不再屬低風險、出現洗錢或恐怖分子資金籌集的懷疑，或者對已有識別或核實資料的真實性或充分性有疑問，即不可採用或繼續簡化盡職審查。', 'SDD has to stop as soon as the conditions for it no longer hold. Stop or do not apply SDD if the risk is no longer low, if money laundering or terrorist financing is suspected, or if there are doubts about the veracity or adequacy of identification or verification information.'),
        ('「不識別、不核實實益擁有人」，是《打擊洗錢條例》附表2第4條的特定例外，並不是「所有低風險客戶都可以免查實益擁有人」。客戶本身、代表，以及其他仍然適用的客戶盡職審查措施，都要繼續履行。例如：即使某名客戶因為屬於合資格金融機構，而可以免查其背後的實益擁有人，機構仍須識別該金融機構本身，並處理其他適用的審查。', 'Omitting identification and verification of beneficial owners is a specific exception under Schedule 2 section 4 of the AMLO. It is not a general waiver for every low-risk customer. Checks on the customer itself and on representatives, and any other applicable CDD measures, still have to be performed. For example: even if beneficial owners behind a qualifying financial institution may be omitted, the institution itself must still be identified, and the other applicable checks remain.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.8.1–4.8.9段', '¶4.8.1–4.8.9', 'it is still required to continuously monitor'),
        ref('04', '附表2第3(1)(e)條', 'Schedule 2 s.3(1)(e)', 'the veracity or adequacy of any information previously'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('可用實益擁有人簡化的客戶', 'Customers eligible for beneficial-owner simplification', [
        ('可以用實益擁有人簡化的客戶類別，是特定的，不是任何「看起來正規」的機構都可以。這些類別包括條例所界定的金融機構；在對等司法管轄區成立、從事類似業務、備有相類的盡職審查及紀錄措施，並受相類監管的機構；股票交易所的上市公司；香港政府或公共機構，以及同等地區的相類機構。對於上市客戶，還須評估其披露要求，是否能夠提供足夠的擁有權透明度。', 'Only specified categories of customer are eligible for beneficial-owner simplification; it is not enough that an institution merely “looks reputable”. Categories include AMLO FIs; comparable institutions established in equivalent jurisdictions, with similar CDD and record measures and similar supervision; listed corporations; and Hong Kong government or public bodies, together with equivalent counterparts in equivalent places. For a listed customer, also assess whether its disclosure requirements provide sufficient beneficial-ownership transparency.'),
        ('投資工具要能確定：負責對全部投資者實施相類客戶盡職審查的人，是合資格的金融機構或受監管機構，而且有可靠的制度。如果投資工具本身，以及獲委任的機構，都不合資格，便須識別並合理核實擁有或控制超過25%權益的投資者，以及其他適用的實益擁有人。', 'For an investment vehicle, ascertain that a qualifying financial institution or supervised institution performs comparable CDD on all investors, and that reliable controls are in place. If neither the vehicle nor the appointed institution qualifies, identify and reasonably verify investors who own or control more than 25%, and any other applicable beneficial owners.'),
        ('擁有權鏈中如果有一個合資格實體，只豁免該實體背後的實益擁有人；與它無關的其他鏈，仍然要識別及合理核實。金融機構代名人帳戶或基金服務帳戶的額外條件，會在下文另列；不能只因為名稱裡有「代名人」或「基金」，便當作已經符合豁免。', 'A qualifying entity in an ownership chain exempts only the beneficial owners behind that entity. Unrelated chains still require identification and reasonable verification. Additional conditions for financial-institution nominee accounts and fund-service accounts appear below; the labels “nominee” or “fund” alone do not qualify.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.8.10–4.8.16段', '¶4.8.10–4.8.16', 'beneficial owners in the ownership chain that are not connected'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('產品及律師客戶戶口例外', 'Product and solicitors’ client-account exceptions', [
        ('產品方面的例外也有嚴格條件。退休計劃須由僱用收入扣款供款，而且規則不准轉讓成員權益；退休計劃保單須沒有退保條款，並且不可用作抵押。人壽保單則須年保費不多於港幣8,000元，或整付保費不多於港幣20,000元。', 'Product exceptions also have strict conditions. A retirement scheme must be funded by deductions from employment income, and its rules must not allow members’ interests to be assigned. A retirement policy must have no surrender clause and must not be capable of being used as collateral. A life policy requires an annual premium of no more than HK$8,000, or a single premium of no more than HK$20,000.'),
        ('律師或律師行的客戶戶口，不是一律都可以免查背後的實益擁有人。只有在戶口以律師或律師行名義持有、把客戶款項或證券混合存放，並且由律師作為代理來管理時，才符合這項例外。如果是單一客戶戶口，或各客戶分戶而不混合款項，則仍須識別底層客戶。例如：律師行一個把多名客戶款項混在一起的客戶帳戶，在符合上述條件時可以免查背後的實益擁有人；如果只是某一個客戶的獨立分戶，便仍須識別該名底層客戶。', 'A solicitor’s or law firm’s client account is not automatically exempt from beneficial-owner checks. A solicitor/firm client account qualifies only if it is held in the solicitor’s name, holds mingled client money or securities, and is managed by the solicitor as the clients’ agent. A single-client account, or segregated subaccounts that do not mingle funds, still require identification of the underlying clients. For example: a firm-wide client account that mingles several clients’ money may, if those conditions are met, omit beneficial-owner identification; a separate subaccount for one client still requires identification of that underlying client.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.8.17–4.8.20段', '¶4.8.17–4.8.20', 'moneys or securities of the customer'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('投資工具及退休計劃例外的責任人', 'Responsible persons for investment-vehicle and retirement exceptions', [
        ('投資工具這項例外裡，負責對全體投資者做相類客戶盡職審查的人，必須是金融機構，或在香港或對等司法管轄區成立、具備打擊洗錢措施、並且受相應監管的相類機構。在法律容許時，可以委任經理、受託人、行政人、過戶代理、登記處或保管人來執行，但仍須有可靠的制度。', 'For the investment-vehicle exception, the person responsible for comparable CDD on all investors must be a financial institution, or a qualifying institution established in Hong Kong or an equivalent jurisdiction, with anti-money-laundering measures and supervised compliance. Where the law permits, a manager, trustee, administrator, transfer agent, registrar or custodian may be appointed, but reliable controls must still be in place.'),
        ('如果沒有符合資格的負責人或獲委任人，可以按風險考慮由負責人按實際所知作出書面陳述，列出擁有超過25%的投資者身分，或確認沒有這樣的人。接受這個做法的理由必須記錄、保存，並定期覆核。這並不免除合理核實，以及其他實益擁有人方面的要求。', 'Where neither the responsible person nor an appointed person qualifies, a risk-based written representation of that person’s actual knowledge may be considered, identifying investors who own more than 25%, or confirming that there is no such investor. The basis for accepting this must be documented, retained and reviewed periodically. Reasonable verification and the other beneficial-owner duties remain.'),
        ('對於合資格的退休計劃，一般可以把僱主視為客戶，並選擇不識別、不合理核實作為該計劃實益擁有人的僱員。如果機構與某名僱員另有獨立的業務關係，則仍須完成該段關係所適用的客戶盡職審查。', 'For a qualifying retirement scheme, the employer may generally be treated as the customer, and identification and reasonable verification of employees as beneficial owners of the scheme may be waived. A separate business relationship with an employee still requires the CDD that applies to that relationship.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.8.10(d)、4.8.14–4.8.18段', '¶4.8.10(d), 4.8.14–4.8.18', 'stating, to its actual knowledge'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('認識：較低風險因素與五類簡化方法', 'Recognise: lower-risk factors and five types of simplification', [
        ('較低風險的客戶例子，見第4.8.7(a)段：香港或對等司法管轄區的政府或公共機構；受充分實益擁有權披露規定約束的上市法團；條例所界定的金融機構，或在對等司法管轄區成立、受符合FATF標準的要求及監督的金融機構；以及在香港或對等地區獲准向公眾發售的集體投資計劃。', 'Examples of potentially lower-risk customers are set out in paragraph 4.8.7(a): Hong Kong or equivalent-jurisdiction government or public bodies; listed corporations that are subject to adequate beneficial-ownership transparency requirements; AMLO financial institutions, or equivalent-jurisdiction financial institutions that are subject to, and supervised for, FATF-consistent requirements; and collective investment schemes authorised for public offering in Hong Kong or an equivalent jurisdiction.'),
        ('產品因素，就是上文已經列出的合資格僱員退休計劃、退休保單及低保費人壽保單，條件和金額都要一併記住。國家因素則是：可靠消息來源指出有有效的打擊洗錢制度，或者貪污或其他犯罪較少。這些只是潛在的較低風險因素，必須作整體評估，不是一見到某類客戶便可以免做客戶盡職審查。', 'The product factors are the qualifying employee retirement schemes, retirement policies and low-premium life policies already listed, and their conditions and amounts must be kept. The country factors are credible-source findings of effective AML/CFT systems, or of lower corruption or other crime. These are potential lower-risk factors that still require a holistic assessment; they are not automatic CDD exemptions.'),
        ('簡化盡職審查的可能方法有五類，見第4.8.8段：（a）對上述客戶接納其他可靠證據，例如金融機構牌照、上市或授權地位；（b）只在第4.8.9至4.8.20段的條件下，簡化實益擁有人審查；（c）降低身分資料更新的頻率；（d）按合理的金額門檻，降低持續監察及交易審查的程度；（e）由交易或關係的類型，推斷目的及擬具有的性質。仍須持續監察，上文所述的停止簡化條件仍然適用。', 'There are five possible methods of simplification in paragraph 4.8.8: (a) alternative reliable evidence for those customers, such as a financial-institution licence, listed status or authorisation status; (b) beneficial-owner simplification only under paragraphs 4.8.9 to 4.8.20; (c) less frequent updates of identity information; (d) reduced monitoring or scrutiny based on a reasonable monetary threshold; and (e) inferring purpose and intended nature from the type of transaction or relationship. Ongoing monitoring remains, and the stop conditions set out above still apply.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.8.2–4.8.8段', '¶4.8.2–4.8.8', 'Examples of possible SDD measures include'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('須記條件：金融機構代名人及基金服務帳戶', 'Remember the conditions: FI nominee and fund-service accounts', [
        ('金融機構代名人帳戶這條路徑，以客戶是條例所界定的金融機構為前提，見第4.8.13段。路徑一：以代名人公司的名義開戶，代該金融機構或其相關客戶持有基金單位；該金融機構須已對其相關客戶進行客戶盡職審查。', 'The financial-institution nominee-account route starts from a customer that is an AMLO financial institution, as set out in paragraph 4.8.13. Route one: an account in a nominee company’s name holds fund units for the financial institution or its underlying customers, and the financial institution must already have conducted CDD on those underlying customers.'),
        ('路徑二：金融機構以投資公司的服務供應商身分，例如基金經理或保管人，以該投資公司的名義開戶；相關投資者無權控制資產管理，而且該金融機構已依照《打擊洗錢條例》對該投資公司進行客戶盡職審查。', 'Route two: the financial institution opens an account in an investment vehicle’s name, acting as that vehicle’s service provider, such as a manager or custodian. The underlying investors have no control over asset management, and the financial institution has conducted AMLO CDD on the investment vehicle.'),
        ('兩條路徑都另外要求，有合約文件或協議證明該金融機構獲授權操作帳戶。只有在符合相應路徑及這項共同條件時，金錢服務經營者才可以選擇不識別、不合理核實該客戶的實益擁有人；其他適用的客戶盡職審查及監察仍然保留。', 'Both routes also require contractual documents or an agreement evidencing the financial institution’s authority to operate the account. Only if the relevant route and this common condition are met may the MSO omit identification and reasonable verification of that customer’s beneficial owners. Other applicable CDD and monitoring remain.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.8.13段', '¶4.8.13', 'in the name of a nominee company'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('enhanced', '加強盡職審查與資金／財富來源', 'Enhanced due diligence and sources of funds/wealth', [
    block('高風險的處理', 'Responding to high risk', [
        ('如果情況本質上屬於高風險，或關長以書面通知顯示高風險，便須採取相稱的加強盡職審查（EDD）。建立或繼續高風險關係，須取得高級管理層批准，並加強持續監察；如果措施仍不足夠，便再以限制交易或戶口功能等方式，減低剩餘風險。', 'Apply proportionate enhanced due diligence (EDD) where the circumstances themselves, or a written notice from the CCE, indicate high risk. Senior approval is required to establish or continue a high-risk relationship, and monitoring must be enhanced. Where residual risk remains, impose further limits or controls, such as limits on transactions or account functions.'),
        ('一般高風險情況，和特定政治人物情況，要求並不相同。一般高風險情況，法例要求管理層批准，再加上確定財富及資金來源，或採其他額外緩解措施。特定政治人物情況則必須完成全部指定措施，不能只任選其中一項。例如：一般高風險客戶，可以在批准之外，用其他額外緩解措施代替確定財富來源；但如果客戶是非香港政治人物，便不能用「選一項額外措施」來代替全部指定要求。', 'General high-risk cases, and specified politically exposed person (PEP) cases, do not have the same requirements. For general high-risk cases the law requires management approval, plus establishing sources of wealth and funds, or other additional mitigation. Specified PEP cases require all of the prescribed measures, rather than a choice of one of them. For example: for a general high-risk customer, other additional mitigation may be used instead of establishing source of wealth, once approval has been obtained. If the customer is a non-Hong Kong PEP, a single optional extra measure cannot replace the full set of prescribed requirements.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.9.1–4.9.6段及註36', '¶4.9.1–4.9.6; footnotes 36', 'no expectation for an MSO to conduct all the examples'),
        ref('04', '附表2第15條', 'Schedule 2 s.15', 'either'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('財富來源與資金來源', 'Source of wealth versus source of funds', [
        ('財富來源（SOW）問的是：這個人的整體資產是怎樣累積起來的，例如事業、投資或繼承所形成的總財富。重點是整個財富體系的來源，而不是只看這一筆錢從哪家銀行轉來。', 'Source of wealth (SOW) asks how the person’s overall body of assets was accumulated, for example through business, investments or inheritance. The focus is the origin of the wealth as a whole, not merely the bank from which a particular sum was sent.'),
        ('資金來源（SOF）問的是：這次關係或交易所涉及的特定資金或資產，是怎樣產生的。只記下「從某銀行轉來」並不足夠，還要了解產生這些資金的活動，以及取得資金的實質理由。例如：客戶說這一筆錢來自某銀行轉帳，還要再問這筆錢是薪金、賣樓，還是其他活動得來的。', 'Source of funds (SOF) asks how the specific money or assets involved in this relationship or transaction were generated. Naming the sending bank alone is not enough; understand the activity that generated the funds, and their substantive provenance. For example: if a customer says that a sum came by a bank transfer, still ask whether that money came from salary, a property sale, or some other activity.'),
        ('採取哪些措施，按風險決定：可以向客戶取得資料，並在有公開的資產或收入申報時加以核對。並非所有官方財產申報都是公開的；客戶沒有交出某一份非公開申報，並不自動證明行為不當。', 'Choose measures according to risk: obtain information from the customer, and corroborate it against public asset or income declarations where those are available. Not every official declaration is public. The absence of a particular non-public declaration is not, by itself, proof of wrongdoing.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.9.24–4.9.26段', '¶4.9.24–4.9.26', 'the origin of an individual'),
    ], kind='comparison'),
    block('現有關係及非經常交易', 'Existing relationships and occasional transactions', [
        ('既有的高風險關係，和單次的高風險非經常交易，條件不能直接互換。根據第15條，繼續一段高風險關係時，除了管理層批准，以及資金或財富來源或其他額外措施之外，如果有實益擁有人，還須合理核實其身分。高風險的非經常交易，則須採取額外緩解措施。例如：要繼續一段已屬高風險的業務關係，不能只做一次額外緩解，便略去對實益擁有人的合理核實。', 'The conditions for an existing high-risk relationship, and for a one-off high-risk occasional transaction, must not be swapped. Under section 15, continuing a high-risk relationship requires reasonable verification of any beneficial owner’s identity, in addition to management approval and source-of-funds or source-of-wealth information, or other additional mitigation. A high-risk occasional transaction requires additional mitigation. For example: continuing an already high-risk business relationship is not completed only by one extra mitigating step, if reasonable verification of the beneficial owner is also required.'),
    ], [
        ref('04', '附表2第15(b)–(c)條', 'Schedule 2 s.15(b)–(c)', 'where an occasional transaction is to be carried out'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('關長書面反制要求可獨立於FATF呼籲', 'CCE written countermeasure requirements can be independent of a FATF call', [
        ('關長可以用書面通知，要求機構採取反制措施，而且這不一定要先有FATF的呼籲。當FATF要求強制加強盡職審查或反制措施，或在其他獨立於FATF呼籲、但屬較高風險的情況，關長都可以書面通知，要求遵從附表2第15條，或採取通知裡指定的反制措施；措施須與風險或缺失的性質相稱。不能把所有反制義務，都只限於某一份FATF名單。', 'A written CCE notice can impose countermeasures, and it does not have to follow a FATF call. Where FATF calls for mandatory EDD or countermeasures, or in other higher-risk circumstances that are independent of a FATF call, the CCE may by written notice require compliance with Schedule 2 section 15, or specific countermeasures set out in the notice, proportionate to the risks or deficiencies. Countermeasure obligations are not limited to one FATF list.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.15.2段', '¶4.15.2', 'independent of any call by the FATF'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('認識完整分類：潛在較高風險因素', 'Recognise the complete groups: potentially higher risks', [
        ('潛在較高風險的客戶因素，前四項是：(1) 業務關係異乎尋常，例如距離遙遠而原因不明，或特定組別在一個或多個地點、或多項服務進行交易；(2) 沒有明確合法商業目的的空殼安排；(3) 有代名人股東或董事，或持票人股份或認股權證；(4) 擁有或經營現金密集業務。', 'The first four potentially higher-risk customer factors are: (1) unusual circumstances of the relationship, such as unexplained geographical distance, or defined groups transacting at one or more locations or across multiple services; (2) shell arrangements without a clear legitimate commercial purpose; (3) nominee shareholders or directors, or bearer shares or warrants; and (4) cash-intensive businesses.'),
        ('客戶因素的後三項是：(5) 架構相對業務性質來說異常，或過度複雜；(6) 對匯款人或收款人詳情所知甚少，或不願披露；(7) 客戶或實益擁有人屬政治人物。政治人物的具體措施，仍須按下文的類別及風險條件來決定，不能只因為這項因素出現，便自動套用全部指定措施。', 'The next three customer factors are: (5) ownership that is unusually or excessively complex for the business; (6) little knowledge of, or reluctance to disclose, originator or recipient details; and (7) a PEP customer or beneficial owner. The specific PEP measures still depend on category and risk, as explained below, and this factor alone does not automatically trigger every prescribed PEP measure.'),
        ('產品、交易或渠道因素的前四項是：(1) 匿名交易，可能涉及現金；(2) 拆單以規避客戶盡職審查或匯款特別規定，從而避開審查或紀錄；(3) 多人匯給一人，或一人匯給多人，而又沒有合理解釋；(4) 經常收到來歷不明，或沒有聯繫的第三方付款。', 'The first four product, transaction or channel factors are: (1) anonymous transactions, possibly involving cash; (2) structuring to avoid CDD or special remittance requirements, and thereby to avoid CDD or records; (3) many-to-one or one-to-many transfers without a reasonable explanation; and (4) frequent payments from unknown or unassociated third parties.'),
        ('產品、交易或渠道因素的後三項是：(5) 與資金來源地或目的地沒有明顯聯繫，而且沒有合理解釋；(6) 代理或交易對手的交易量，與整體或過往一般水平不一致；(7) 代理的合規計劃未達標準。', 'The next three product, transaction or channel factors are: (5) no apparent ties to the origin or destination of the funds, and no reasonable explanation; (6) agent or counterpart volume that is inconsistent overall, or relative to typical past volume; and (7) substandard agent compliance programmes.'),
        ('國家方面的潛在較高風險因素有四項，而且是用來作整體評估的例子，不是自動定罪的規則。這四項是：可靠來源指出打擊洗錢及恐怖分子資金籌集制度欠有效；貪污或其他犯罪程度高；受聯合國等的制裁、禁令或類似措施；或向恐怖活動提供資金或支持，以及有指定恐怖組織在當地活動（這項的英文連詞是 or）。清單並非盡列。', 'There are four country factors, and they are non-exhaustive risk examples for a holistic assessment, not automatic proof of crime. The four country factors are credible-source findings of ineffective AML/CFT systems; significant corruption or other crime; sanctions, embargoes or similar measures, for example by the UN; or funding or support for terrorism, or designated terrorist organisations operating there. The English connector in that last factor is “or”.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.9.5段及註35', '¶4.9.5; footnote 35', 'Examples of potentially higher risk factors'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('理解如何履行：六類可能的EDD措施', 'Understand implementation: six possible EDD measures', [
        ('可能採取的加強盡職審查措施，先記前三類：（a）索取額外的客戶資料，例如職業、資產量及公開資料，用來做風險分析，並更頻密地更新客戶及實益擁有人資料；（b）補充了解這段關係擬具有的性質；（c）取得財富來源及資金來源資料。', 'Possible EDD measures can first be remembered in three groups: (a) obtain additional customer information, such as occupation, volume of assets and public information, to inform risk profiling, and update customer and beneficial-owner information more frequently; (b) obtain additional information on the intended nature of the relationship; and (c) obtain source-of-wealth and source-of-funds information.'),
        ('另外三類是：（d）查明擬進行或已進行交易的原因；（e）評估資金目的地，以及交易原因的資料；（f）要求首次付款，經由客戶本人在遵守相類客戶盡職審查標準的銀行帳戶進行。第4.9.6段及註36並不要求每宗高風險關係都做齊這六個例子；應按風險選擇相稱的措施，但不能藉此略去政治人物等另有規定的必須措施。', 'The other three are: (d) obtain the reasons for intended or completed transactions; (e) evaluate information on the destination of funds and the reasons for the transactions; and (f) require the first payment to pass through the customer’s own account at a bank that is subject to similar CDD standards. Paragraph 4.9.6 and note 36 do not require all six examples for every high-risk relationship. Choose proportionate measures, but do not omit separately prescribed duties, such as applicable PEP measures.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.9.6段及註36', '¶4.9.6; footnote 36', 'Examples of possible EDD measures'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('財富來源：甚麼情況須深入了解', 'Source of wealth: when deeper understanding is required', [
        ('不是每名客戶都要一律確立財富來源。常見問題解答並不要求對每名客戶一律確立財富來源。它列舉的高風險情況包括：客戶或實益擁有人屬非香港政治人物；與香港或國際組織政治人物客戶或實益擁有人的高風險關係；以及在適當時，其他本質上高風險的情況。政治人物所需的全部措施，見下一節。', 'Source of wealth does not have to be established for every customer. The FAQ does not expect source-of-wealth establishment for every customer. Its high-risk examples include a non-Hong Kong PEP customer or beneficial owner, a high-risk relationship with a Hong Kong or international-organisation PEP customer or beneficial owner, and, where appropriate, other inherently high-risk situations. The complete PEP measures are in the next section.'),
        ('對於非高風險客戶，職業或公司業務性質等已經取得的資料，通常應足以理解客戶狀況，並用來監察戶口結餘、交易金額及交易量，是否與預期的財富或背景相符。高風險客戶也不必全部使用同一套程序；在風險不足以支持時，無須收集數十年前的證據。這是按風險決定查證的深度，不是免除應做的財富來源審查。', 'For a customer who is not high-risk, existing information such as occupation or the nature of the company’s business should often provide a basic profile, against which account balances and transaction values or volumes can be monitored. High-risk customers need not all go through identical procedures. Evidence from decades ago is not expected where the risk does not justify it. This sets a risk-sensitive depth of enquiry; it is not an exemption from required source-of-wealth work.'),
    ], [
        ref('06', '打擊洗錢問答A16', 'AML/CFT FAQ A16', 'collect evidence dating back decades'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('peps', '政治人物：類別、親屬及加強措施', 'Politically exposed persons: categories, associates and measures', [
    block('政治人物的範圍', 'Who is a PEP', [
        ('非香港政治人物，是在香港以外獲委以重要公職的人，現任或曾任都包括在內。例子包括國家或政府首長、高級政界、政府、司法或軍方人員、國有企業高層，以及重要政黨官員；不包括中級或初級人員。', 'A non-Hong Kong PEP is a person who holds, or has held, a prominent public function outside Hong Kong. Examples include heads of state or government, senior politicians, government, judicial or military officials, senior executives of state enterprises, and important party officials. Middle-ranking or junior officials are excluded.'),
        ('香港政治人物，是在香港擔任或曾經擔任重要公職的人，例如政府首長、資深從政者、高級政府或司法官員、政府擁有企業的高級行政人員，以及重要政黨幹事；同樣不包括中級或更低級官員。國際組織政治人物，包括獲委重要職能的董事、副董事、董事會成員，或同等的高級管理人員，同樣不包括中級或更低級官員。', 'A Hong Kong PEP is a person who holds, or has held, a prominent public function in Hong Kong, including heads of government, senior politicians, senior government or judicial officials, senior executives of government-owned corporations, and important party officials. Middle-ranking or more junior officials are excluded. An international-organisation PEP holds, or has held, a prominent function, including as a director, deputy director, board member or equivalent senior manager, and middle-ranking or more junior officials are likewise excluded.'),
        ('範圍還包括配偶或伴侶、子女、父母、子女的配偶或伴侶，以及關係密切的人。密切聯繫包括緊密的業務關係、共同實益擁有法人或信託，或者實益擁有為該政治人物的利益而設立的法人或信託。', 'The scope also includes spouses or partners, children, parents, children’s spouses or partners, and close associates. Close association includes close business relations, joint beneficial ownership of a legal person or trust, or beneficial ownership of a legal person or trust set up for the PEP’s benefit.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.9.7–4.9.8、4.9.13–4.9.15段', '¶4.9.7–4.9.8, 4.9.13–4.9.15', 'a spouse or a partner of a child'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('三類政治人物的措施', 'Measures by category', [
        ('如果客戶或實益擁有人是非香港政治人物，須在建立關係之前，或在既有關係中發現這個身分之後、繼續往來之前，完成指定措施：取得高級管理層批准、合理確定財富及資金來源，並加強持續監察。這三項都要做，不是只選其中一項。', 'If the customer or a beneficial owner is a non-Hong Kong PEP, the prescribed measures must be completed before the relationship is established, or before it is continued after the PEP status is discovered in an existing relationship. For a non-Hong Kong PEP customer/beneficial owner, obtain senior management approval, reasonably establish the sources of wealth and funds, and enhance ongoing monitoring. All three are required; they are not alternatives.'),
        ('香港或國際組織政治人物的處理方法，與非香港政治人物並不完全相同。須採取合理措施識別香港或國際組織政治人物。只在建立高風險關係、既有關係變成高風險，或在高風險關係中發現其身分時，才須採取上述全部加強盡職審查措施。不是每一位本地政治人物都一律自動屬高風險。例如：一名本地政治人物經評估後不一定屬高風險關係，但仍須先被識別出來；不能把「不是自動高風險」理解成可以完全不做識別。', 'Hong Kong and international-organisation PEPs are not treated in exactly the same way as non-Hong Kong PEPs. Take reasonable steps to identify Hong Kong or international-organisation PEPs. Apply all of the enhanced measures above when establishing a high-risk relationship, when an existing relationship becomes high-risk, or when PEP status is discovered within a high-risk relationship. Local PEP status is not an automatic, universal high-risk classification. For example: a local PEP may, after assessment, not have to be treated as a high-risk relationship, but the person must still first be identified. “Not automatically high-risk” does not mean identification can be skipped.'),
        ('一個人卸任，並不會自動解除這些措施，法律也沒有統一規定「過了若干年便可以免」。須評估殘餘影響力、原來職位的高低，以及前後職能之間的聯繫；只有在信納不再屬高風險，並且取得管理層批准之後，才可以不採用或停止指定的加強盡職審查，而且須保留評估紀錄。', 'Stepping down from office does not, by itself, switch the measures off, and there is no universal rule that a set number of years is enough. Leaving office does not automatically end the measures, and there is no universal elapsed-time exemption. Assess residual influence, the seniority of the former role, and the links between former and current functions. Cease the prescribed EDD only with a documented finding that there is no continuing high risk, and with senior approval.'),
        ('商業資料庫只是輔助工具，不能取代了解職業、僱主等正常的客戶盡職審查。使用時須明白資料庫可能不完整、定義並不一致，而且有技術限制。對親屬和密切聯繫，也須按風險調整加強盡職審查的程度。', 'A commercial database is a support tool; it does not replace ordinary CDD, such as enquiries about occupation or employer. Understand that databases can be incomplete, that definitions may be inconsistent, and that there are technical limits. For family members and close associates, also tailor the intensity of EDD according to risk.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.9.9–4.9.12、4.9.16–4.9.23段及註37–42', '¶4.9.9–4.9.12, 4.9.16–4.9.23; footnotes 37–42', 'not merely on prescribed time limits'),
    ], kind='comparison'),
    block('國際組織及批准人員的定義界線', 'International organisations and who can approve PEP relationships', [
        ('這裡所說的國際組織，須由成員國以正式政治協議設立，該協議具有國際條約地位，其存在獲成員國法律承認，而且不是所在地的居民機構單位；聯合國機構屬於這一類。不是所有名稱裡有「國際」二字的體育或民間組織都符合；不過，那些組織裡的職位，仍可能影響客戶風險。', 'An international organisation, in this sense, is established by formal political agreements between member states that have the status of international treaties, is legally recognised in the member countries, and is not a resident institutional unit of its host country. United Nations agencies qualify. An international sports or civil association does not qualify merely because of its name, although positions in such a body may still affect customer risk.'),
        ('批准政治人物關係的人，必須有足夠的高級職權，而且金錢服務經營者須把這項安排清楚寫在政策裡。職銜及人數，按組織規模、類型和機構風險而定。如果與組織結構及風險管理安排相符，也可以包括境外的高級管理層；並不是必須指定一個通用職銜。', 'A person who approves a PEP relationship must have sufficient seniority, and the MSO must record this clearly in its policy. Titles and numbers depend on the institution’s size, type and risk. Overseas senior personnel may qualify where that is consistent with the organisational structure and with risk management. No universal job title is prescribed.'),
    ], [
        ref('06', '打擊洗錢問答A18–A19、A21', 'AML/CFT FAQ A18–A19, A21', 'formal political agreements'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('remote', '非親身識別：額外措施與數碼例外', 'Non-face-to-face identification: extra measures and digital exception', [
    block('至少一項額外措施', 'At least one additional measure', [
        ('如果客戶沒有親身在場接受識別，除了下文的獲承認數碼識別例外之外，至少還要再做一項額外措施：用未曾用於核實的獨立來源再核實一次；採取補充措施，驗證已經取得的資料；或確保第一筆付款，經由客戶本人在認可機構或合資格同等地區機構的戶口進行。', 'If identification takes place without the customer being physically present, at least one extra measure is required, unless the recognised-digital-identification exception applies. If the customer was not physically present for identification, apply at least one additional measure unless that exception applies: further verification using independent evidence that has not already been used; supplementary checks on the information already obtained; or ensuring that the first payment is made through the customer’s own account at an authorised institution, or at a qualifying equivalent institution.'),
        ('這裡所說的合資格境外機構，須在對等司法管轄區成立、從事相類的銀行業務、具備相類的客戶盡職審查及紀錄措施，並且受相類監管。這項要求針對的是「付款」，並不是只有「存款」才計算在內。例如：第一筆錢是從客戶本人在合資格銀行的戶口付出，用來完成一筆匯款，這仍然可以是這裡所說的「付款」。', 'The overseas institution must be established in an equivalent jurisdiction, conduct comparable banking business, maintain similar CDD and record measures, and be comparably supervised. The requirement concerns a payment, not only a deposit. It is not limited to cases in which the first movement is a deposit into an account. For example: a first transfer paid out from the customer’s own account at a qualifying bank, to complete a remittance, can still be a “payment” for this purpose.'),
        ('如果已經使用關長承認、而且屬可靠獨立來源的數碼識別系統資料，核實了身分，便可以免去上述額外措施。一般的視像通話，或機構自行選用的電子平台，並不會自動等同獲承認的系統。', 'The extra measures are waived where identity has been verified using a reliable, independent digital identification system that is recognised by the CCE. An ordinary video call, or an electronic platform that the institution has simply chosen for itself, is not automatically such a system.'),
        ('補充措施可以包括由合資格人士核證、查閱可靠資料庫或登記冊，或使用適當的科技，但須逐案確保足以防止冒認。如果非自然人客戶是由遠端代表建立關係，或只提供公司文件副本，同樣須緩減因此增加的風險。', 'Supplementary measures may include certification by a suitable person, checks against a reliable database or register, or appropriate technology, assessed case by case against the risk of impersonation. Increased risk must also be mitigated where a non-individual customer is onboarded through a remote representative, or only through copies of company documents.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.10.1–4.10.5段', '¶4.10.1–4.10.5', 'not required to carry out any additional measures'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('核證作為補充措施的範圍', 'Scope of certification as a supplementary measure', [
        ('如果選擇把核證，當作附表2第9條的補充措施，一般核證的是用作身分核實的文件，例如身分證、護照、公司註冊證書或職權證明書。並不要求把客戶交來的所有其他盡職審查資料或文件，一律都拿去核證；如果機構可以與公開來源核對，也沒有一律核證的要求。', 'If certification is chosen as a supplementary measure under Schedule 2 section 9, it generally covers documents used for identity verification, such as identity cards, passports, certificates of incorporation or certificates of incumbency. Certification is not expected for every other piece of CDD information or document, or where the MSO can check the documents against public sources.'),
        ('常見問題解答的中英文本，對出示正本的說法並不完全相同。中文本說應盡量容許有意的客戶向職員出示正本；英文本說應一直給予此機會。實際安排應讓客戶有機會出示正本，而不是堅持只能付費取得核證副本。如果採用核證，仍須遵守本部分「身分文件與核證副本」一節的核證人及程序要求。', 'The Chinese and English FAQs do not use identical wording about presenting originals. The Chinese FAQ says to allow willing customers to present originals as far as possible; the English says they should always be given that opportunity. Provide an opportunity to show originals, instead of insisting only on paid certification. Certification still follows the certifier and procedure requirements in the “Identity documents and certified copies” section above.'),
    ], [
        ref('06', '打擊洗錢問答A27', 'AML/CFT FAQ A27', 'There is no expectation to require certification for all other'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('intermediaries', '依賴中介人：條件與不可轉移責任', 'Reliance on intermediaries: conditions and retained responsibility', [
    block('依賴與外判的分別', 'Reliance versus outsourcing', [
        ('依賴中介人，和外判或代理，不是同一種安排。中介人通常自己已有獨立的客戶關係，並按其自身程序做客戶盡職審查；外判或代理則按本機構的程序進行，並受本機構控制。無論哪一種安排，最終的客戶盡職審查責任，始終由本機構承擔。', 'Reliance on an intermediary is not the same arrangement as outsourcing or agency. An intermediary normally has its own independent customer relationship and applies its own procedures. Outsourcing or agency applies the MSO’s procedures under the MSO’s control. In either case, ultimate CDD responsibility stays with the MSO.'),
        ('可以依賴中介人執行的，是附表2第2條的部分或全部客戶盡職審查，但不能把第5條的持續監察責任也交給中介人。例如：可以讓合資格中介人先完成開戶時的身分核實，但此後對交易是否異常的持續監察，仍須由本機構自己負責。', 'An intermediary can be relied on for some, but not all, of the CDD duties. Reliance may cover any part of s.2 CDD, but not the MSO’s s.5 ongoing-monitoring responsibility. For example: a qualifying intermediary may complete identity verification at onboarding, but ongoing monitoring of whether transactions are unusual remains the MSO’s own responsibility.'),
        ('須取得書面確認，證明中介人同意，以及同意承擔哪些措施，並且信納對方可以按要求、不延誤地提供文件。有關措施完成後，須立即取得中介人所收集的資料或資訊；不必在同一時間取得全部底層文件的副本。', 'Written confirmation is required, not merely an informal understanding. Obtain written confirmation of consent and agreed measures, and be satisfied that documents will be supplied on request without delay. Obtain the collected data or information immediately after the measure is completed; simultaneous copies of every underlying document are not required.'),
        ('還須取得承諾，在關係期間，以及關係完結後至少5年，或關長指定的較長期間，保留底層的客戶盡職審查資料，並且抽查可否及時供應。終止依賴時，須立即取回全部資料；如果對中介人的可靠性有疑問，便須覆核該中介人，並補做所需的客戶盡職審查。', 'Also obtain an undertaking to retain the underlying CDD information for the duration of the relationship and for at least five years afterwards, or any longer period specified by the CCE, and sample-test whether the information can be retrieved in time. On termination, obtain all of the information immediately. If there is doubt about the intermediary’s reliability, review the intermediary and perform any necessary CDD.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.11.1–4.11.7段及註44', '¶4.11.1–4.11.7; footnotes 44', 'does not apply to outsourcing or agency relationships'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('可依賴的類別', 'Eligible categories', [
        ('可以依賴的本地中介人類別是特定的，不是任何金錢服務經營者都因此自動合資格。本地類別包括：認可機構、持牌法團、獲授權保險人及指定的持牌保險中介；以及會計、地產及法律專業人士與信託或公司服務提供者（TCSP）持牌人，但這些專業人士及持牌人須備有充分的防洗錢程序，並且就該名客戶須遵守附表2的相關要求。', 'Only specified categories of domestic intermediary may be relied on; being an MSO does not, by itself, automatically qualify. Domestic: authorised institutions, licensed corporations, authorised insurers and specified licensed insurance intermediaries; and accounting, estate-agency and legal professionals and TCSP licensees, provided they have adequate controls and, for that customer, the applicable Schedule 2 duties. MSO status alone does not automatically qualify.'),
        ('要確定本地中介人符合準則，第4.11.9段列出可以採取的措施，包括：(a) 如屬會計專業人士、地產代理、法律專業人士或信託或公司服務提供者持牌人，確定其是否須就有關客戶遵從附表2的相關規定；(b) 查詢其聲譽，或任何集團層面打擊洗錢或恐怖分子資金籌集標準的應用及審核程度；或 (c) 覆核其打擊洗錢或恐怖分子資金籌集的政策及程序。', 'To confirm that a domestic intermediary meets the criteria, paragraph 4.11.9 sets out measures that may include: (a) for an accounting professional, estate agent, legal professional or TCSP licensee, ascertaining whether it must comply with the relevant Schedule 2 requirements for the customer; (b) enquiring about its stature, or the extent to which any group AML/CFT standards are applied and audited; or (c) reviewing its AML/CFT policies and procedures.'),
        ('境外可以依賴的，是在對等司法管轄區經營的相類金融機構、律師或公證人、審計、會計或稅務顧問、信託或公司服務提供者、信託公司，或相類地產代理，而且須受註冊、發牌或規管，具備相類措施，並受監督。', 'Overseas intermediaries that may be relied on are comparable financial institutions, lawyers or notaries, auditors, accountants or tax advisers, TCSPs, trust companies, or comparable estate agents, operating in an equivalent jurisdiction, and subject to registration, licensing or regulation, similar measures, and supervision.'),
        ('另外還有一條「關連境外金融機構」的路徑，須符合指定的集團或分支關係、集團政策、相類措施，以及集團層面監管等條件，詳見下一段。', 'There is a separate route for a related foreign financial institution. It requires the prescribed group or branch relationship, group policy, comparable measures, and group-level supervision, which are set out next.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.11.8–4.11.14段', '¶4.11.8–4.11.14', 'an institution that carries on a business similar'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('相關境外金融機構的三種關係', 'Three relationship routes for a related foreign FI', [
        ('這條關連路徑裡的機構，必須在境外經營相類的金融機構業務，並且屬於以下三者之一：(1) 與金錢服務經營者同一集團的公司；(2) 在香港成立，或符合第04份所存版本所指經遷冊資格的金錢服務經營者的境外分行；(3) 在境外成立、而且並非經遷冊實體的金錢服務經營者的總辦事處，或該總辦事處的分行。不能僅僅因為有商業合作，便把對方當成「相關境外金融機構」。', 'The institution on this related route must conduct similar financial-institution business abroad, and must be one of the following: (1) a same-group company, (2) an overseas branch of a Hong Kong-incorporated or qualifying re-domiciled MSO, or (3) the head office, or a head-office branch, of a foreign-incorporated MSO that is not a re-domiciled entity. Ordinary commercial cooperation does not establish this related-foreign-FI status.'),
        ('集團政策必須同時適用於本機構及該境外機構，要求實施相類的客戶盡職審查、備存紀錄及打擊洗錢計劃，並且符合有關當局，或對等司法管轄區相類主管的集團層面監管條件。政策須緩解所在地較高的國家風險，並定期以獨立覆核查核持續遵從情況。', 'The group policy must apply to both the MSO and that institution, requiring similar CDD, record-keeping and anti-money-laundering programmes, together with qualifying group-level supervision by a relevant authority or an equivalent-jurisdiction counterpart. It must address higher country risk, and regular independent review of ongoing compliance must be obtained.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.11.12–4.11.14段', '¶4.11.12–4.11.14', 'it is a branch of the head office of the MSO'),
        ref('04', '附表2第18(7)條', 'Schedule 2 s.18(7)', 'related foreign financial institution'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('本地中介人的保險及專業類別', 'Insurance and professional categories of domestic intermediary', [
        ('本地中介人的具體類別包括：持牌個人保險代理、持牌保險代理機構、持牌保險經紀公司；會計類包括註冊會計師、執業法團及會計師事務所；地產類包括持牌地產代理及營業員；法律類包括香港律師及註冊外地律師；另有信託或公司服務提供者持牌人，包括法定當作持牌者。即使職銜符合，仍須符合前文相應類別關於附表2、該名客戶，以及充分防洗錢程序的條件，不能只憑職銜便加以依賴。', 'The specific domestic categories include licensed individual insurance agents, insurance agencies and insurance broker companies; accounting professionals, including certified public accountants, corporate practices and firms; estate professionals, including licensed estate agents and salespersons; legal professionals, including Hong Kong solicitors and registered foreign lawyers; and TCSP licensees, including statutory deemed licensees. The applicable Schedule 2, customer-specific and adequate-procedure conditions set out above still apply; a title alone is not enough.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.11.8段', '¶4.11.8', 'a licensed individual insurance agent'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('持續監察可獲協助，但不能轉移責任', 'Ongoing monitoring: assistance without transferring responsibility', [
        ('依賴中介人的法定路徑範圍有限。如上文所述，法定依賴只涵蓋附表2第2條的客戶盡職審查，並不能把第5條的持續監察交出去。不過，中介人可以協助收集更多文件、數據及資料，並提供或協調更新。本機構仍須確保自己保存的盡職審查紀錄，現時有效而且相關。', 'Statutory reliance has a limited reach. Statutory reliance on an intermediary covers Schedule 2 section 2 CDD, as already noted, and does not transfer section 5 monitoring. The intermediary may nevertheless assist by collecting further documents, data and information, and by providing or coordinating updates. The MSO remains responsible for ensuring that its own CDD records are up to date and relevant.'),
    ], [
        ref('06', '打擊洗錢問答A22', 'AML/CFT FAQ A22', 'provide or coordinate relevant updates'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('monitoring', '持續監察與原有客戶', 'Ongoing monitoring and pre-existing customers', [
    block('持續CDD及交易監察', 'Ongoing CDD and transaction monitoring', [
        ('持續的客戶盡職審查，是不時更新客戶資料，使資料保持相關及最新；並不是每次覆核都要重新核實已經確認的身分，除非對舊資料產生疑問。高風險客戶至少每年覆核一次。對於休眠客戶，現有的盡職審查紀錄不必作定期覆核，但關係重新啟用時應覆核；政策及程序應清楚界定何謂休眠客戶。', 'Ongoing CDD means keeping customer information relevant and current. It does not require routine re-verification of an identity that has already been verified, unless doubts arise about the old information. Review high-risk customers at least annually. Regular review of a dormant customer’s existing CDD records is unnecessary, but a review should be carried out when the relationship is reactivated. Policies and procedures should clearly define what a dormant customer is.'),
        ('交易監察有兩方面，缺一不可。一方面檢查交易與客戶業務、風險及資金來源是否一致，另一方面識別複雜、異常大額，或呈異常模式、而且沒有明顯經濟或合法目的的交易，調查其背景及目的，並把結果書面記錄。', 'Transaction monitoring has two sides, and both matter. Monitoring checks consistency with the customer’s business, risk and sources of funds, and also identifies complex, unusually large, or unusual-pattern transactions that have no apparent economic or lawful purpose, examining their background and purpose and recording the findings.'),
        ('監察宜從整段關係來看，跨越不同戶口及關連客戶，而不是只逐筆分開來看。參數包括金額或頻率、相連的系列、對手、資金的來源地或目的地，以及平常的戶口活動，並且須定期覆核及作獨立驗證。', 'Prefer a holistic view of the relationship, across accounts and related customers, rather than looking at isolated transactions. Parameters include amount or frequency, series of transactions, counterparties, geographical origin or destination, and normal account activity, and they should be reviewed regularly and independently validated.'),
        ('有兩類情況，任何一類出現，都須作適當查詢：交易與客戶背景不符，或屬異常而且沒有明顯目的的活動。如果解釋令人滿意，可以不再採取進一步行動，但仍應考慮更新風險；如果不能滿意解釋，而且已經形成懷疑，便須向聯合財富情報組舉報，並記錄結果及理由。', 'Either of two situations calls for appropriate enquiries. Either profile inconsistency or unusual activity lacking an apparent purpose must be followed up. A satisfactory explanation may mean that no further action is required, but the risk rating may still need to be updated. If the explanation cannot be accepted and suspicion arises, report to the JFIU and document the findings and reasons.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第5.1–5.14段及註52–53', '¶5.1–5.14; footnotes 52–53', 'preferably the MSO adopts a relationship-based approach'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('2012年4月1日前建立的關係', 'Relationships established before 1 April 2012', [
        ('在現行規定生效前已經建立關係的原有客戶，並不是從此可以永久免做客戶盡職審查。如果出現異常或可疑交易，或交易與已知背景、業務、風險或資金來源不符，或戶口運作有重大改變，或出現懷疑，或質疑原有資料，便須進行審查。休眠關係重新啟用，或實益擁有人或控制權有改變，也可以構成觸發事件。持續監察則一直適用。', 'Pre-existing customers are not permanently exempt from CDD. CDD is triggered by unusual or suspicious transactions, or by transactions that are inconsistent with the known profile, business, risk or source of funds, by material changes in how the account is operated, by suspicion, or by doubts about the old information. Reactivation of a dormant relationship, or a change in ownership or control, may also trigger a review. Ongoing monitoring always applies.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.12.1–4.12.3段', '¶4.12.1–4.12.3', 'before the AMLO came into effect on 1 April 2012'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('監察制度設計與資料供應', 'Monitoring-system design and information access', [
        ('監察制度的設計、自動化程度及精密程度，須按業務規模及複雜度、風險、現有系統及管控、其他業務監察程序，以及產品和交付方式而定，並不是一律強制採用自動化系統。須及時向負責監察或調查的相關員工，提供足夠資料，讓他們識別及分析客戶交易。', 'How the monitoring system is designed, and how automated or sophisticated it is, depends on the size and complexity of the business, the risk, the existing systems and controls, other business monitoring, and the products and delivery methods. Automation is not universally mandated. Staff responsible for monitoring or investigation need timely and sufficient information to identify and analyse customer transactions.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第5.4–5.5段', '¶5.4–5.5', 'timely and sufficient information required to identify, analyse and effectively monitor'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('screening', '制裁及恐怖分子篩查', 'Sanctions and terrorist screening', [
    block('資料庫、時間與處理', 'Database, timing and response', [
        ('須建立並更新恐怖分子及受指定人士的資料庫，涵蓋香港憲報、商務及經濟發展局以及海關提示的名單。可以使用第三方資料庫，但須抽查其是否完整及準確。聯合國如有新名單，應盡快加入，不能等到香港完成立法，才開始處理相關風險。', 'Maintain and update a database of terrorists and designated persons, covering designations in the Gazette and those notified by the Commerce and Economic Development Bureau (CEDB) and by Customs and Excise (C&ED). Third-party databases may be used, but completeness and accuracy must be checked. Add new United Nations lists promptly, without waiting for Hong Kong implementation before the risk is addressed.'),
        ('建立關係時，須篩查客戶及實益擁有人；名單有新增或更新後，須盡快再查一次；執行跨境電傳或匯款之前，須篩查全部相關人士。即使客戶風險被評為低，仍須篩查。關連人士及代表，則按風險為本方法延伸處理。', 'Screen customers and beneficial owners when the relationship is established, and again promptly after a designation is added or updated. Before executing a cross-border wire or remittance, screen all relevant parties. Screening applies even to low-risk customers. Extend it to connected parties and representatives on a risk-based approach.'),
        ('如果只是姓名相似，須先加強核查，確認是否真正命中，並保存篩查及核查結果。一旦有恐怖分子資金籌集、擴散資金籌集或違反制裁的懷疑，便須向聯合財富情報組舉報。即使把篩查或名單維護外判給海外辦事處，最終責任仍在本機構。', 'A similar name is not automatically a confirmed match. Investigate potential name matches to determine whether there is a genuine hit, and keep the screening and check results. Report suspicions of terrorist financing, proliferation financing or sanctions breaches to the JFIU. Outsourcing screening or database maintenance to an overseas office does not transfer ultimate responsibility.'),
        ('法律禁止進行的交易，和按風險採取加強盡職審查，是不同層次的要求。不能因為風險評為低，便忽略仍然適用的制裁禁令。如要取得合法特許，須按相應法例向保安局或商務及經濟發展局申請，詳見第1部分。', 'A legal prohibition is not the same thing as risk-based enhanced due diligence. A low-risk rating does not override an applicable sanctions prohibition. Licensing exceptions require the competent Security Bureau or CEDB process under the relevant law, as explained in Part 1.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第6.6–6.8、6.12–6.19段及註58', '¶6.6–6.8, 6.12–6.19; footnotes 58', 'irrespective of the risk profile attributed to the customer'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('匯款篩查的六組最低相關方', 'Six minimum groups of relevant payment parties for screening', [
        ('跨境電傳或匯款，至少要篩查以下六組相關方：(1) 匯款人；(2) 收款人；(3) 匯款機構；(4) 中介機構；(5) 收款機構；(6) 付款訊息中列名的人士，例如個人、公司及銀行。對客戶及實益擁有人的篩查仍須完成，不能只查匯出銀行或收款人。例如：只核對了收款銀行的名稱，卻沒有篩查匯款人、收款人及訊息裡列名的其他人士，並不符合這項最低要求。', 'For a cross-border wire or remittance, at a minimum screen these six groups: (1) the originator; (2) the recipient; (3) the ordering institution; (4) any intermediary institution; (5) the beneficiary institution; and (6) named parties in the payment message, such as individuals, companies and banks. Screening of the customer and beneficial owners remains necessary; checking only the sending bank or the recipient is not enough. For example: matching only the beneficiary bank’s name, without screening the originator, the recipient and other parties named in the message, does not meet this minimum.'),
    ], [
        ref('06', '打擊洗錢問答A24', 'AML/CFT FAQ A24', 'named parties'),
        ref('07', '附錄(2)第4頁', 'Appendix (2), p.4', 'irrespective of the risk profile'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('2018年制裁通函：兩語強度差異及共同要求', '2018 sanctions circular: language difference and common requirements', [
        ('2018年制裁通函第2頁的中英文本，強度並不完全相同。中文寫，列入聯合國安理會制裁決議或名單「已足以構成知悉或懷疑的理由」，法定責任（包括呈報）及罪行條文隨即適用；英文寫 may constitute grounds（可能構成理由）。依擁有人2026年10月20日的決定，保留兩語原文的強度差異，不擅自改成相同措辭，也不要把英文的「可能」理解為可以忽略名單。', 'The Chinese and English versions of page 2 of the 2018 sanctions circular are not identical in strength. Page 2 of document 26 says inclusion in a UNSC sanctions resolution or list “may constitute grounds for knowledge or suspicion”, triggering statutory obligations (including reporting) and offence provisions. The Chinese text says inclusion is already sufficient grounds, and those provisions immediately apply. Under the owner’s 20 October 2026 decision, retain this difference rather than silently harmonising the wording; “may” is not permission to disregard a list.'),
        ('兩種文本仍有共同要求：聯合國公布後，須在實際可行情況下盡快篩查所列國家、個人、實體及活動，不論香港是否已經實施相應制裁；同時仍須履行客戶盡職審查、持續監察，以及法定的知悉或懷疑報告責任。名單資料庫不論由內部還是外部供應，金錢服務經營者都須負責及時更新。如果只是單純同名，須先查明是否真正命中，見本節上文。', 'The two versions still share common requirements. Both versions require screening listed countries, people, entities and activities as soon as practicable after the United Nations promulgates the list, regardless of whether Hong Kong has implemented the corresponding sanctions, alongside CDD, ongoing monitoring and the statutory knowledge or suspicion reporting duties. The MSO remains responsible for timely database updates, whether the database is maintained internally or by an external provider. A mere name match must still be investigated to establish whether there is a genuine hit, as explained above.'),
    ], [
        ref('26', '第2頁，(d)後段落及第2節末段（續第3頁）', 'p.2, paragraph after (d), and end of section 2 (continuing on p.3)', 'may constitute grounds for knowledge or suspicion'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('third-party-payments', '第三方付款：例外接受與嚴格管控', 'Third-party payments: exceptional acceptance and strict controls', [
    block('接受條件及審查', 'Acceptance conditions and checks', [
        ('這裡所說的第三方，是指客戶以外的人。由第三方付款，可能會掩蓋真正的實益擁有人或資金來源，因此應認真考慮拒絕。如果沒有足夠措施管理這種固有的高風險，並且符合有關規定，便不應接受。', 'A third party, in this context, is anyone other than the customer. Payment by a third party can conceal the true beneficial owner or the source of funds, so refusal should be considered seriously. Do not accept the payment where adequate measures cannot manage the inherent high risk and meet the requirements.'),
        ('只有在例外、而且情況合法、又合理符合客戶背景及正常商業做法時，才可以接受第三方付款，並且須依據高級管理層批准的詳細政策，以及嚴格的管理批准來執行。政策的五項內容見下文。', 'Accept a third-party payment only exceptionally, in legitimate circumstances that are reasonably consistent with the customer’s profile and with normal commercial practice, and only under detailed policies approved by senior management and under stringent management approval. The five policy components are set out below.'),
        ('接受之前，須評估付款原因及是否有必要；按風險合理核實第三方的身分，以及與客戶的關係；並由負責打擊洗錢的高級管理層批准，同時記錄查詢、佐證及批准。要記住，這個第三方本身，也可能就是真正的實益擁有人。', 'Before accepting, assess the rationale and the necessity of the payment; reasonably verify the third party’s identity and relationship with the customer on a risk-sensitive basis; obtain approval from senior management responsible for anti-money laundering; and document the enquiries, corroboration and approval. The payer may in fact be the true beneficial owner.'),
        ('相對較低風險的例子，包括直系親屬、客戶的實益擁有人或聯屬公司，以及受規管的金融機構，但這些都不是自動豁免。較高風險則須加強審查，並確定相關資金來源；如果關係難以核實、付款前沒有身分資料，或同一人替多名互不相關的客戶收付款，便尤其須小心。例如：丈夫為妻子支付一筆合理的家庭匯款，可能屬於較低風險的例子，但仍須按政策評估，不是自動可以接受。', 'Examples of relatively lower risk include immediate family, the customer’s beneficial owners or affiliates, and regulated financial institutions; none of these is an automatic exemption. Higher risk requires enhanced scrutiny and establishment of the source of funds, especially where the relationship cannot be verified, identity information is missing before payment, or one person pays or receives for many unrelated customers. For example: a husband paying for a reasonable family remittance by his wife may be a lower-risk illustration, but it still has to be assessed under the policy and is not automatically acceptable.'),
        ('應鼓勵客戶指定本人名下的銀行戶口，以便辨識資金來源，詳見下文。同時加強持續監察及員工培訓，向客戶清楚說明拒收或例外接受的政策，以及所需文件；一旦形成懷疑，便須向聯合財富情報組舉報。', 'Encourage customers to designate bank accounts in their own names, as explained below, so that the source of funds can be identified. Enhance ongoing monitoring and staff training, explain the rejection and exception policies and the document requirements clearly to customers, and report any suspicion to the JFIU.'),
    ], [
        ref('08', '第4–6頁，主要措施第1–12項及註6', 'pp.4–6, key controls 1–12; footnote 6', 'only under exceptional and legitimate circumstances'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('須認識：第08份列出的八項警號', 'Recognise: the eight red flags listed in document 08', [
        ('文件08列出八項警號，先記前兩項：(1) 交易與對客戶的認知或交易目的不符，例如匯款與經濟活動、來源地或人士不相稱；(2) 多名客戶看似合謀，把一項交易拆成兩項或以上低於客戶盡職審查門檻的交易。', 'Document 08 lists eight red flags. The first two are: (1) transactions that are incompatible with knowledge of the customer or with the purpose of the transaction, such as a mismatch between remittances and the economic activity, place of origin or person; and (2) multiple customers who appear to be cooperating in splitting one transaction into two or more transactions below the CDD thresholds.'),
        ('接下來兩項是：(3) 多名看似無關的客戶，集中採用相同的交易模式，例如都轉往同一個個人帳戶；(4) 大額金錢轉入或轉出香港境外，並指示以現金支付；如果匯款人或收款人是辦理一次性交易的非居民街客，情況更可疑。', 'The next two are: (3) seemingly unrelated customers who concentrate on the same transaction pattern, such as transfers to one individual’s account; and (4) large sums moving to or from outside Hong Kong with instructions for cash payment, especially where a single transaction is instructed by a walk-in non-resident originator or recipient.'),
        ('再接下來是：(5) 客戶代表第三方交易，卻沒有適當的業務關係；(6) 多名看似無關的客戶，授權同一個不是受規管人士或實體的第三方，透過已建立的業務關係，向金錢服務經營者發出各種活動指示。', 'The next two are: (5) a customer transacting for a third party without an appropriate business relationship; and (6) many seemingly unrelated customers authorising the same third party, who is not a regulated person or entity, to instruct the MSO on activities through their established relationships.'),
        ('最後兩項是：(7) 由第三方資助的頻繁或大額轉帳，沒有可信的商業理由或解釋；(8) 客戶不能按要求立即提供額外的身分證明文件。如果付款人姓名是第三方，或匯款與通常業務或活動不符，便應要求解釋匯款的性質。這八項只是非盡列的警號，須作跟進評估；不能把任何一項直接等同已經證明洗錢。', 'The last two are: (7) frequent or large transfers funded by a third party, without a credible commercial rationale or explanation; and (8) customers who cannot immediately provide additional identification documents as required. A third-party payer name, or a remittance that is inconsistent with usual business or activity, calls for an explanation of the nature of the remittance. These eight flags are illustrative and non-exhaustive, and they require follow-up assessment; none of them automatically proves laundering.'),
    ], [
        ref('08', '「可疑交易訊號／潛在較高風險因素」，第2–3頁', 'Red flags/potentially higher risk factors, p.3', 'a single individual’s account'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('第三方付款政策：五項內容與識別付款來源', 'Third-party payment policy: five components and identifying payment sources', [
        ('通函要求，有關政策或程序應獲高級管理層批准，並處理以下五項等內容：(a) 可例外接受的合法情況及評估準則；(b) 識別資金形式第三方付款的監察系統及管控；(c) 在適用時，判斷付款是否符合接受準則的盡職審查程序；(d) 加強監察涉及第三方付款的客戶帳戶，並向聯合財富情報組報告所識別的懷疑；(e) 負責執行各項政策或程序的指定經理或職員。制度應向相關職員有效傳達，並以嚴格的合規監察來落實。', 'The circular says that policies and procedures should be approved by senior management and should address, among other matters: (a) the exceptional legitimate circumstances in which acceptance is allowed, and the assessment criteria; (b) monitoring systems and controls that identify third-party payments in the funds; (c) where applicable, due diligence for assessing the acceptance criteria; (d) enhanced monitoring of the affected client accounts, and reporting of identified suspicions to the JFIU; and (e) designated managers or staff responsible for implementation. The systems should be communicated effectively to relevant staff, and enforced through robust compliance monitoring.'),
        ('要識別是否第三方付款，通函舉例應向客戶取得銀行結單、付款通知等佐證。海關強烈鼓勵要求客戶指定其本人名下的銀行帳戶，作所有付款之用，以便在執行第三方付款前確認來源，並完成必要審查。這是強烈鼓勵的做法，不能改寫成法例一律禁止其他付款方式。員工指引應有可接受付款人的例子，客戶亦應清楚獲告知拒收或例外接受政策，以及佐證要求。', 'To establish whether a payment comes from a third party, the circular gives the example of obtaining the customer’s bank statements or advice slips. Customs strongly encourages requiring customers to designate own-name bank accounts for all payments, which helps identify the source and complete the necessary due diligence before a third-party payment is effected. This is strongly encouraged practice, not a statutory blanket ban on all other payment methods. Staff guidance should include examples of acceptable payers, and customers should be clearly informed of the rejection and exception policies and of the supporting-document requirements.'),
    ], [
        ref('08', '主要管控措施第2、4–5、10–12項及註5（第3–5頁）', 'Key controls 2, 4–5, 10–12 and footnote 5 (pp.4–6)', 'the respective designated managers'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('delivery', '交付渠道、代理及境外對手風險', 'Delivery channels, agents and overseas counterpart risk', [
    block('加入渠道前與持續覆核', 'Before engagement and during the relationship', [
        ('在使用海外代理或對手之前，須先全面評估風險。建立或維持與客戶、業務伙伴及對手的關係時，還要評估整條交付渠道被濫用的程度，並定期重新檢視當地監管要求及新出現的風險。', 'Do not appoint an overseas agent or counterpart first and assess the risk only afterwards. Assess comprehensively before engaging overseas agents/counterparts. When establishing or maintaining relationships with customers, partners and counterparts, assess the vulnerability of the delivery channel as a whole, and regularly review regulatory requirements and emerging risks.'),
        ('還要明白資金如何移動、代理如何結算，以及消費者資金不獲履約、或在境外被凍結的風險。渠道一旦有改變，須反映在機構的風險評估及內控制度裡；對高風險客戶或交易，須採取加強盡職審查。', 'Also understand how funds move, how agents settle, and the risks of non-performance or of customer funds being frozen overseas. Channel changes must be reflected in the institution’s risk assessment and internal controls, and EDD must be applied to high-risk customers or transactions.'),
        ('如果境外的某項行為，假如發生在香港便會構成可公訴罪行，其得益仍可能受香港的洗錢罪涵蓋，並不取決於當地是否同樣把該行為列為違法。一旦有知悉或懷疑，仍須向聯合財富情報組舉報。例如：某筆資金來自境外一項在當地未必被檢控的行為，但同一行為若在香港會屬可公訴罪行，便仍可能落入香港洗錢罪的範圍。', 'Proceeds of overseas conduct may still fall within Hong Kong money-laundering law, if that conduct would have been an indictable offence had it taken place in Hong Kong. This does not depend on whether the conduct is also unlawful in the place where it occurred. Knowledge or suspicion still triggers reporting to the JFIU. For example: funds that come from overseas conduct which may not be prosecuted locally can still fall within Hong Kong laundering law, if the same conduct would have been an indictable offence in Hong Kong.'),
    ], [
        ref('14', '第1–2頁及註4', 'pp.1–2 and footnote 4', 'before engaging other parties in its business model'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('wire-transfers', '電傳轉帳：定義及發出機構資料要求', 'Wire transfers: definition and ordering-institution information', [
    block('範圍與豁除', 'Scope and exclusions', [
        ('電傳轉帳，是發出機構代表發款人，以電子方式令款項可供發款人本人，或另一受款人，在受益機構取得。中間可以有中介機構，也可以在同一機構的不同分行之間進行。機構須按自己在這條鏈中所擔當的角色來履責。', 'A wire transfer is an electronic transfer through an ordering institution, making money available at a beneficiary institution for the originator or for another recipient. It can involve intermediary institutions, or branches of the same institution. Duties depend on the role the institution is performing in the chain.'),
        ('如果機構本身就是發款人或受款人，便不是以發出、中介或受益機構的角色行事。金錢服務經營者與金融機構，或與境外相類機構之間的轉帳，如果雙方都是為自己行事，便屬於第12條的豁除範圍。', 'An MSO that is itself the originator or the recipient is not acting in an ordering, intermediary or beneficiary role. Transfers between an MSO and a financial institution, or a comparable foreign institution, where both sides are acting for themselves, are excluded from section 12.'),
        ('信用卡、扣帳卡或預付卡交易要獲豁除，必須同時符合幾個條件：該轉帳是由這類卡交易產生、該卡並不是用作人對人轉帳的付款系統，以及轉帳訊息附有卡號或等同的識別碼。不能把所有用卡付款的轉帳，一律當成已經豁除。', 'The card exclusion applies only if several conditions are met together: the transfer arises from a credit, debit or prepaid-card transaction; the card is not used as a person-to-person payment system; and the transfer message includes the card number or an equivalent identifier. It does not exclude every transfer that happens to be funded by a card.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第10.1–10.4段', '¶10.1–10.4', 'the card is not used as a payment system'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('港幣8,000元的界線', 'The HK$8,000 boundary', [
        ('電傳轉帳在港幣8,000元這條界線上，所需資料並不相同。達港幣8,000元或以上，須附發款人的姓名、戶口或可追蹤編號，以及地址，或客戶識別碼，或證件號碼，或（如屬自然人）出生日期及地點；另外還要附受款人姓名，以及戶口或受益機構編號。所需的發款人資料必須準確。', 'The information that must travel with a wire is not the same on both sides of the HK$8,000 line. At least HK$8,000: carry originator name and account or traceable reference, plus address, or a customer identification number, or an identity-document number, or, for an individual, date and place of birth; also carry the recipient’s name and account or beneficiary-institution reference. Required originator information must be accurate.'),
        ('低於港幣8,000元，並不是完全不需要任何資料。仍須附上雙方姓名，以及各自的戶口或參考編號。對於非經常交易的發款人，一般不必核實身分，但如果相連交易的總額已達門檻，或出現懷疑，則仍須核實。', 'A wire below HK$8,000 still cannot travel with no information at all. It must still carry both names, and each side’s account or reference number. An occasional originator generally need not be verified, unless linked transactions reach the threshold, or suspicion arises.'),
        ('同一發款人的批量跨境轉帳，可以在個別指示裡只附其戶口或編號，但批次檔必須載有準確、完整、而且可追蹤的所需雙方資料。本地電傳可以把發款人資料簡化為可追蹤的發款人戶口號碼；如無戶口，則用獨特參考號碼；所需的受款人資料仍須隨附。應接收電傳指示的機構或關長要求，須在收到要求後3個營業日內提供完整發款人資料；應執法機構要求，則須立即提供。', 'In a cross-border batch for the same originator, the individual instructions may carry only the originator’s account or reference number, but only if the batch file contains the required accurate, complete and traceable information on both sides. A domestic wire may abbreviate originator data to a traceable originator account number, or to a unique reference where no account exists; required recipient data must still accompany the transfer. Supply full originator data within three business days after receiving a request from the institution that received the instructions, or from the CCE, and immediately on a law-enforcement request.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第10.5–10.13段及註70–71', '¶10.5–10.13; footnotes 70–71', 'within 3 business days after the request is received'),
    ], kind='comparison'),
    block('匯款人資料的準確性與地址', 'Accuracy of originator information and usable addresses', [
        ('按《打擊洗錢條例》及指引核實了匯款人身分之後，所需的匯款人資料便視為準確，通常不必再逐項核實；但在個別個案中，仍可酌情作進一步核查。隨附的地址須足以識別所在位置，以便作制裁篩查及監察；除了沒有其他地址可用之外，應避免只用郵政信箱。', 'Once the originator’s identity has been verified under the AMLO and the Guideline, the required originator information is deemed accurate, and normally needs no further item-by-item verification, although additional checks may still be made in a particular case. An accompanying address should be enough to identify the location, for screening and monitoring. Avoid using only a post-office box, unless no alternative address exists.'),
    ], [
        ref('06', '打擊洗錢問答A25–A26', 'AML/CFT FAQ A25–A26', 'except where no alternative exists'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('戶口號碼、客戶識別號碼、交易參考號碼', 'Account number, customer identifier and transaction reference', [
        ('有相關戶口時，須使用該戶口號碼；只有在沒有該戶口時，才使用由相應匯款機構或收款機構編配、可追查該筆交易的獨特參考號碼。這項先後條件，同時適用於匯款人及收款人的所需資料，不是可以任意選一個方便的號碼。例如：客戶在本機構已有戶口，付款訊息便應使用該戶口號碼，而不是另編一個內部參考號碼來代替。', 'Use the relevant account number when one exists. Only if there is no such account may the traceable unique reference assigned by the appropriate ordering or beneficiary institution be used. This order of priority applies to the required information on both the originator and the recipient; it is not a free choice of whichever number is convenient. For example: if the customer already has an account with the institution, the payment message should carry that account number, and not a separately invented internal reference in its place.'),
        ('客戶識別號碼，是機構用來唯一識別匯款人的號碼，必須指向一份紀錄，而該紀錄至少載有以下其中一項：地址、身分證明文件號碼，或出生日期及地點。獨特交易參考號碼，則是用來追查該筆交易。兩者不是同一種號碼。', 'A customer identification number uniquely identifies the originator to the institution, and must point to a record containing at least one of the following: an address, an identification-document number, or date and place of birth. A unique transaction reference traces the transaction itself. The two identifiers serve different purposes.'),
        ('直接撥付機制（cover payment，例如 MT202COV 付款）仍然要遵守本章適用的電傳要求。這只是付款機制的名稱，不是「掩蓋付款」或洗錢的同義詞。匯款機構還須有有效程序，防止匯出不合規的電傳：合理檢查本地或跨境轉帳所需雙方資料是否缺漏，按風險處理缺漏的轉帳，並及時修補管控上的缺失，包括在適當時作定期的內控或審核測試。', 'Cover-payment mechanisms, such as MT202COV payments, remain subject to the applicable Chapter 10 wire-transfer requirements. The term names a payment mechanism; it is not a synonym for concealment or money laundering. Ordering institutions also need effective procedures to prevent non-compliant outgoing wires: reasonable checks for missing required information on both sides of domestic or cross-border transfers, risk-based handling of incomplete transfers, and timely repair of control gaps, including appropriate regular control or audit testing.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第10.3、10.5–10.7、10.13段及註70', '¶10.3, 10.5–10.7, 10.13; footnotes 70', 'is a different number from the unique transaction reference number'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('wire-receiving', '電傳轉帳：中介及受益機構責任', 'Wire transfers: intermediary and beneficiary duties', [
    block('本地轉帳的範圍及兩層資料要求', 'Domestic scope and two levels of information requirements', [
        ('「本地」電傳，不能只看發款人和受款人在哪裏。匯款機構、收款機構，以及每一間中介機構，都必須是位於香港、而且符合《打擊洗錢條例》定義的金融機構。只要鏈中出現境外中介機構，便不符合這項本地電傳的定義。例如：發款人和受款人都在香港，但如果中間經過一間境外銀行，這筆轉帳便不再屬於這裡所說的本地電傳。', 'Whether a wire is “domestic” is not decided only by where the originator and the recipient are. The ordering institution, the beneficiary institution and every intermediary must be financial institutions as defined by the AMLO, and they must all be located in Hong Kong. An overseas intermediary takes the chain outside this domestic-wire definition. For example: even if both the originator and the recipient are in Hong Kong, a transfer that passes through an overseas bank is no longer a domestic wire in this sense.'),
        ('本地電傳其實有兩層資料要求，不能只記較窄的法例文字，便忽略指引。條例附表2第12(6)及(9)條允許本地轉帳隨附發款人戶口或獨特參考號碼，收款機構則須追索缺漏的該號碼。文件03第10.11至10.12段只簡化發款人資料，並沒有免除所需的受款人資料；第10.20段還要求收款機構追索本地或跨境轉帳中，雙方缺漏的所需資料。這兩層要求都要分開認識：較窄的法例文字，並不能成為可以忽略指引的理由。', 'Domestic wires in fact have two layers of information requirements, and the narrower statutory wording must not be used to ignore the Guideline. Schedule 2 sections 12(6) and (9) permit the originator account or unique reference number to accompany a domestic wire, and require the beneficiary institution to obtain that number if it is missing. Document 03 paragraphs 10.11 to 10.12 simplify originator information, without exempting the required recipient information; paragraph 10.20 requires the beneficiary institution to obtain missing required information on either side, for domestic or cross-border wires. Recognise both levels: the narrower statutory wording does not justify ignoring the Guideline.'),
    ], [
        ref('04', '附表2第12(6)、(9)、(11)條', 'Schedule 2 s.12(6), (9), (11)', 'domestic wire transfer'),
        ref('03', '第10.11–10.12、10.20段及註71', '¶10.11–10.12, 10.20; footnote 71', 'Domestic wire transfer means'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('資料傳遞、缺漏與核實', 'Pass-through, missing data and verification', [
        ('中介機構須保留，並向下一站傳遞全部隨附的發款人及受款人資料。如果因為技術限制，無法在跨境轉帳與相連的本地轉帳之間保留這些資料，應至少保存所收到的資料5年；相反方向的情況，同樣適用。', 'An intermediary must retain, and pass on to the next institution, all accompanying originator and recipient information. If technical limitations prevent that information remaining with a linked domestic or cross-border transfer, the information received should be kept for at least five years, and the same applies in the reverse direction.'),
        ('中介機構和收款機構，識別缺漏資料的方法並不完全相同。中介機構須採用與直通式處理一致的合理措施，以識別跨境電傳欠缺的資料；收款機構則須識別本地或跨境電傳欠缺的資料，例如可以用事後監察等合理措施。兩者都須有按風險決定執行、拒絕、暫停及跟進的政策，並在合理可行範圍內盡快向上一手機構取得適用的欠缺資料。如果取不到，中介機構「應考慮」、收款機構「須考慮」限制或終止與該機構的關係，或採取合理的緩減措施。', 'Intermediaries and beneficiary institutions do not identify missing data in exactly the same way. Intermediaries use reasonable measures consistent with straight-through processing to identify missing data in cross-border wires. Beneficiary institutions identify missing data in domestic or cross-border wires, for example through post-event monitoring. Both need risk-based policies on whether to execute, reject, suspend or follow up, and both must obtain applicable missing data from the preceding institution as soon as reasonably practicable. If the data cannot be obtained, the intermediary should consider, and the beneficiary institution should consider (the Chinese text says 須考慮), restricting or ending the relationship with that institution, or taking reasonable mitigating measures.'),
        ('如果已知資料不完整或沒有意義，須盡快採取合理措施減低風險。對於達港幣8,000元或以上的轉帳，受益機構如果此前尚未核實受款人，便應核實其身分。', 'Where information is known to be incomplete or meaningless, prompt and reasonable mitigation is required. For transfers of at least HK$8,000, a beneficiary institution should verify a recipient who has not already been verified.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第10.14–10.22段', '¶10.14–10.22', 'incomplete or meaningless'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('remittances', '非電傳匯款：發款人與必備紀錄', 'Non-wire remittances: originator and required records', [
    block('匯款的特別要求', 'Special remittance requirements', [
        ('「匯款」和「電傳轉帳」不是同義詞。匯款交易，是把錢送往或安排送往香港以外的地方；電傳轉帳，則是按電子機構鏈來定義。屬於電傳的，按第12條處理；非電傳的對外匯款，則按第13條處理。', '“Remittance” and “wire transfer” are not synonymous. A remittance sends, or arranges to send, money outside Hong Kong. A wire transfer is defined by the electronic institutional chain. Apply section 12 to wires, and section 13 to non-wire outward remittances.'),
        ('非電傳的對外匯款，如果達港幣8,000元或等值外幣，須在執行前，用身分文件識別及核實發款人。發款人是提供款項的戶口擁有人；如果沒有戶口，則是發出指示的人。例如：顧客以現金委託一筆港幣8,000元、不是經電傳鏈處理的對外匯款，執行前便須核實發款人，不能只記住一般非經常交易的港幣120,000元門檻。', 'A non-wire outward remittance has its own threshold, which is not the general occasional-transaction figure of HK$120,000. Before a non-wire outward remittance of at least HK$8,000 or equivalent, identify and verify the originator using an identity document. The originator is the holder of the account that funds the remittance or, if there is no account, the person who gives the instructions. For example: a customer who tenders cash for a HK$8,000 outward remittance that is not processed through a wire chain must be identified and verified before execution; the general HK$120,000 occasional-transaction threshold is not the relevant line here.'),
        ('還須在執行前，記錄發款人姓名、證件號碼（如果是旅行證件，還要另記簽發地）、地址、幣種及金額；指示的接收日期及時間、受款人姓名及地址，以及交付方式。這些資料須可供關長查閱。', 'Before execution, also record the originator’s name, identity-document number (and, for a travel document, the place of issue), address, currency and amount, the date and time when the instruction was received, the recipient’s name and address, and the delivery method. The information must be available to the CCE.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第11.1–11.6段', '¶11.1–11.6', 'date and time of receipt of the instruction'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('第13條的識別文件', 'Identification documents for section 13', [
        ('第13條所說的個人「識別文件」，範圍是特定的，不能把其他場合可接受的證件直接搬過來用。法定識別文件包括身分證、身分證明書、簽證身分書及旅行證件。在某些一般的非親身客戶盡職審查情況可以接受的國民駕駛執照，並不會因此就成為第13條的指定識別文件。', 'The “identification document” for an individual under section 13 is a defined list, and a document that is acceptable in another CDD context cannot automatically be used here. It includes an identity card, a certificate of identity, a document of identity, or a travel document. A national driving licence acceptable in some general remote-CDD cases is not thereby a section 13 identification document.'),
    ], [
        ref('04', '附表2第1、13條', 'Schedule 2 ss.1, 13', 'certificate of identity'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('trade-based-laundering', '貿易洗錢：定義與四類風險指標', 'Trade-based money laundering: definition and four indicator groups', [
    block('概念及使用指標的方法', 'Concept and use of indicators', [
        ('貿易洗錢（TBML）是利用貿易交易，掩飾犯罪得益或轉移價值，使非法來源看起來合法，或資助非法活動。常見手法包括虛假貿易、錯報價格、數量或品質、重複單據，或使用空殼公司。實際貨物、合約、單據與付款，應能合理地互相對應。', 'Trade-based money laundering uses trade transactions to hide criminal proceeds or to move value, so that an illegal origin looks legitimate, or so that illegal activity can be financed. TBML disguises criminal proceeds and moves value through trade, including through fictitious trade, misreported price, quantity or quality, duplicate documents, and shell companies. Goods, contracts, documents and payments should have a reasonable relationship to one another.'),
        ('風險指標只是警號，單獨一項並不能證明已經犯罪。清單並非盡錄，機構也未必能看到全部資料。須連同客戶、交易，以及可以取得的外部資料，作整體判斷；如果多個指標同時出現，便應提高關注，並及時呈報管理層。', 'Indicators are warning signs, not proof on their own. The lists are not exhaustive, and an MSO may not be able to observe every piece of data. Assess the customer, the transaction and any available external information as a whole. Where several indicators appear together, greater concern is warranted, and the matter should be escalated to management in a timely way.'),
    ], [
        ref('18', '第1–3頁', 'pp.1–3', 'trade-based money laundering'),
        ref('24', '第1–2頁（中文為學習譯文）', 'pp.1–2', 'By no means is this a conclusive list'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('結構及業務活動指標', 'Structural and business-activity indicators', [
        ('結構方面的指標包括：不合理的複雜架構或空殼；在打擊洗錢合規薄弱的地區設立或設辦事處；地址看來供大量公司登記（例如密集住宅、郵箱，或商業、工業大廈，尤其是沒有單位號碼），或與業務不符而又沒有合理解釋；人手與貿易量不相稱、名義擁有人不了解業務、網站空泛或欠缺、名稱模仿知名企業、無法解釋的休眠期，或有負面情報。這裡所說的「集中註冊地址」，不是指「短期內有大量公司來註冊」。', 'Structural indicators include illogical complexity or shell companies; registration or offices in a jurisdiction with weak AML/CFT compliance; an address that appears to be used for mass registration (dense housing, a post box, or a commercial or industrial building, especially without a unit number), or an address that is inappropriate for the business without explanation; staffing inconsistent with trade volume; uninformed nominees; generic or absent websites; imitation names; unexplained dormancy; or adverse information. A mass-registration address is not a claim about a large number of recent registrations.'),
        ('活動方面的指標包括：貨物或規模與業務不符、不必要的中介人或迂迴航線、不合理的低利潤，或超過自身能力的交易、突然出現龐大融資、新設或重啟的企業在高門檻行業突然做巨額交易，以及不必要地複雜的貿易融資。', 'Activity indicators include goods or a scale that is inconsistent with the business, unnecessary intermediaries or routes, implausibly low margins or trade beyond the firm’s capacity, sudden large funding, a new or reactivated business that suddenly trades in large amounts in a high-entry-barrier sector, and unnecessarily complex trade finance.'),
    ], [
        ref('24', '印刷第3–4頁', 'Printed pp.3–4', 'Structural risk indicators'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('單據／貨物及帳戶／付款指標', 'Document/goods and account/payment indicators', [
        ('單據或貨物方面的指標包括：合約、發票及付款上的名稱並不一致；數量、品質或市場價格不符；描述過於籠統；單據偽造、遺失、反覆修改，或被拒後再重交；進口貨值與相應的對外銀行轉帳不符，或出口貨值與境外來款不符。另外還有兩項須分開記清楚：貨物在暫時進口或進料加工制度下進口，之後卻用偽造單據出口；以及沒有明顯經濟理由，而經多個司法管轄區運送。', 'Document or goods indicators include inconsistent names across contracts, invoices and payments; discrepancies in quantity, quality or market value; vague descriptions; false, missing, repeatedly modified, or resubmitted documents; imported trade values that are inconsistent with the corresponding outward bank transfers, or exported trade values that are inconsistent with incoming foreign transfers. Distinguish two further situations: goods imported under temporary-importation or inward-processing arrangements and later exported using falsified documents; and goods routed through several jurisdictions without apparent economic justification.'),
        ('帳戶或付款方面的指標包括：臨時改收款人、日期或金額；營業額與背景不符；資金快速進出而且餘額很低；不相干的第三方付款；分拆以避開門檻；突然放量之後又休眠；以及不尋常的整數和循環轉帳。', 'Account or payment indicators include last-minute changes of beneficiary, date or amount; turnover inconsistent with the profile; rapid pass-through with little remaining balance; unrelated third-party funding; splitting to stay below a threshold; a spike in activity followed by dormancy; unusual round amounts; and circular flows.'),
    ], [
        ref('24', '印刷第5–6頁', 'Printed pp.5–6', 'Account and transaction activity'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('發現風險後的措施', 'Response to identified risks', [
        ('發現風險後，須按風險加強客戶盡職審查，查詢交易目的以及資金或財富來源，並核對貨物、業務能力、單據及對手。不能因為客戶隨便給一個解釋，便結束監察警報。如果無法合理解釋而形成懷疑，須盡快向聯合財富情報組舉報，包括嘗試進行但尚未完成的交易，而且不受金額限制；同時覆核原有監控是否有缺口。', 'Once a risk has been identified, enhance CDD on a risk-sensitive basis, enquire into the purpose of the transaction and the source of funds or wealth, and check the goods, the firm’s capacity, the documents and the counterparties. Do not close an alert merely because the customer offers an unsupported explanation. If suspicion arises because no reasonable explanation can be given, report promptly to the JFIU, including attempted or uncompleted activity, and irrespective of value; also review whether there are gaps in the existing controls.'),
    ], [
        ref('18', '加強措施第1–4項', 'Enhancements 1–4', 'attempted transactions'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('營運支出與所稱業務不符', 'Operating outgoings inconsistent with the claimed business', [
        ('如果聲稱的業務規模，理應會有正常的薪酬、營運開支或稅款交易，卻看不到這些支出，這可以成為一項結構風險線索。須連同整體背景及合理解釋一起評估；單一指標並不等於已經證明洗錢。', 'An absence of ordinary payroll, operating-cost or tax transactions, where that absence is inconsistent with the claimed scale of the business, can be a structural warning sign. Assess it together with the full context and any reasonable explanation. A single indicator is not proof of laundering.'),
    ], [
        ref('24', '印刷第3頁，結構風險指標', 'Printed p.3, Structural risk indicators', 'it lacks regular payroll transactions'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('2026年通函：核實新設實體及交易真實性', '2026 circular: checking new entities and transaction genuineness', [
        ('應特別留意新成立、又缺乏顯著資產、員工及／或活躍業務運作的法人客戶，主動考慮反欺詐程序，審查客戶資料以核實交易真實性，並評估匯款人或收款人是否空殼公司。這是風險及真實性審查，不能只核對成立證明，也不是把所有新公司一律拒收。', 'Pay particular attention to newly established legal entities that lack significant assets, employees and/or active business operations. Proactively consider anti-fraud procedures, scrutinise customer information to verify that the transaction is genuine, and assess whether the originator or recipient is a shell. This examines risk and genuineness beyond incorporation evidence; it is not a blanket rejection of every new company.'),
        ('評估交易是否合理，應合看客戶風險、資金或財富來源，以及歷史交易。如果同時掌握匯款人及收款人的資料，在決定是否提交可疑交易報告（STR）時，應把兩邊資料一併考慮。不能因為付款方檔案看起來合格，便不再理會收款方的警號；疑似交易仍須連同懷疑根據一起報告。', 'Assess whether a transaction is reasonable by looking together at customer risk, source of funds or wealth, and transaction history. If information is held on both the originator and the recipient, take all of it into account when deciding whether to file a suspicious transaction report (STR). A satisfactory file on the payer is not a reason to disregard red flags on the recipient side. Report suspected activity together with the matters that support the suspicion.'),
    ], [
        ref('18', '2026年1月20日通函第2–4項（第1–2頁）', '20 January 2026 circular, items 2–4 (p.2)', 'proactively consider to apply anti-fraud procedures'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('貿易指標的具體例子與價格比較限制', 'Specific trade indicators and limits of price comparisons', [
        ('結構或文件方面的警號，還包括不履行通常的業務申報責任（原文以增值稅申報為例），以及複雜或經常性的貿易，卻採用異常簡單、像網上樣本的合約。這些是全球報告裡的例子，不能把增值稅申報誤寫成香港每家金錢服務經營者的稅務要求；也不能只因為文件看起來齊全，便忽略它是否與業務相稱。', 'Further structural or document indicators include non-compliance with ordinary business filing obligations (the source gives VAT returns as an example), and unusually simple, internet-template-like contracts used for complex or regular trade. These are examples from a global report, not a VAT-filing requirement for every Hong Kong MSO. Documents that look complete still need to be consistent with the actual business.'),
        ('「不合理低利潤」的例子，包括批發進貨價已經達到或超過零售價，或持續以等於或低於成本的價格出售。判斷時可能須估計貨品的公平價格；沒有公開市場交易的貨品較難估價，原文註5明確保留這個限制。應把可靠市價、交易條件及其他背景合起來看，不能單憑猜測價格，便認定是洗錢。', 'Examples of unreasonably low margins include wholesale purchases at or above retail value, or consistent resale at or below cost. The assessment may require an estimate of a fair commodity price. Footnote 5 specifically recognises the difficulty of doing this for commodities that have no open market. Consider reliable prices, transaction terms and context together, rather than treating a guessed price as proof of laundering.'),
    ], [
        ref('24', '印刷第3–5頁及註5（中文為學習譯文）', 'Printed pp.3–5 and footnote 5', 'determining the profit margin'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('suspicion-indicators', '其他可疑交易指標', 'Other suspicious-activity indicators', [
    block('使用方法：記住分類，理解具體警號', 'Use: remember the groups and understand the indicators', [
        ('第7.10段把43項非盡列的警號分成六組。學習時要能認識具體模式，以及它為什麼可疑，不必逐字背誦例句。單一警號並不是定罪，或自動必須提交可疑交易報告的充分條件。按照第7.10段末的要求，須作進一步調查，至少初步查詢資金來源，並要求額外的盡職審查佐證；一旦形成知悉或懷疑，便須按第7部分的法定及內部程序盡快報告。', 'Paragraph 7.10 sets out 43 non-exhaustive indicators in six groups. Learn to recognise the specific patterns and why they matter; it is not necessary to memorise the examples word for word. A single indicator is not proof, and is not an automatic trigger for an STR. Under the closing words of paragraph 7.10, investigate further, at least by making initial source-of-funds enquiries and requesting additional CDD evidence. Where knowledge or suspicion is formed, report promptly through the statutory and internal procedures in Part 7.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第7.9–7.11段', '¶7.9–7.11', 'list of non-exhaustive red flag indicators'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('一、不合經濟常理的交易：九項', '1. Transactions without economic sense: nine indicators', [
        ('第一組是「不合經濟常理的交易」，共九項。前四項是：(1) 模式與客戶的正常活動不符；(2) 與對客戶的認知、經驗或交易目的不符，例如經濟活動、來源地或人士與所收匯款不相稱；(3) 頻密交易被刻意分拆到客戶盡職審查門檻以下，以免留下紀錄；(4) 化整為零或分拆（structuring／smurfing）：本來可以用一宗或幾宗大額交易完成，卻改作多宗小額。看來相連的操作，仍須合併起來計算門檻。', 'The first group is transactions without economic sense, and it has nine indicators. The first four are: (1) a pattern inconsistent with the customer’s normal activity; (2) incompatibility with knowledge or experience of the customer, or with the purpose of the transaction, for example a mismatch between the economic activity, origin or person and the remittances received; (3) frequent, deliberate splitting below CDD thresholds in order to avoid records; and (4) structuring or smurfing: many smaller transactions where one or a few larger ones could have been used. Operations that appear linked still have to be aggregated for threshold purposes.'),
        ('同一組的接下來兩項是：(5) 折返交易（U-turn）：境外某人或公司的來款，再匯至同一境外司法管轄區的另一人或公司，或匯至原匯款人在另一司法管轄區的戶口；(6) 不必要地經多間金融機構或人士轉款。', 'The next two in the same group are: (5) a U-turn, where funds from a foreign person or company are remitted on to another person or company in that same foreign jurisdiction, or to the sender’s account in another jurisdiction; and (6) unnecessary routing through multiple financial institutions or people.'),
        ('最後三項是：(7) 交易頻率或金額突然增加，又沒有合理解釋，尤其是涉及新的收款人或目的地；(8) 多名匯款人匯入同一個個人戶口；(9) 客戶與收款人沒有明顯關係，及／或私人匯款的目的地與客戶沒有明顯的家庭或商業聯繫，及／或匯出地或收款地與客戶無關，而且不能充分解釋原因。', 'The last three are: (7) an unexplained sudden increase in frequency or value, particularly involving new destinations or people; (8) many senders remitting to one individual’s account; and (9) no apparent relationship between the customer and the recipient, and/or personal remittances that lack apparent family or business ties to the destination, and/or no connection between the customer and the sending or receiving jurisdiction, without a sufficient explanation.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第7.10(a)段', '¶7.10(a)', '“Structuring” or “Smurfing”'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('二、現金：七項', '2. Cash: seven indicators', [
        ('第二組是現金，共七項。前三項是：(1) 與個人或業務背景不符的頻密大額現金交易；(2) 大額或頻密的匯款，看似與客戶業務無關；(3) 把大量小面額鈔票，兌換成另一貨幣的大面額鈔票。', 'The second group is cash, and it has seven indicators. The first three are: (1) frequent large cash transactions that are not justified by the individual or business background; (2) large or frequent remittances that appear unrelated to the customer’s business; and (3) unusually large exchanges of small-denomination notes for high-denomination notes in another currency.'),
        ('其餘四項是：(4) 尤其在短期內，多宗交易每一筆都低於客戶盡職審查門檻，或單筆金額不大，但合計卻很龐大，或已經超過門檻；(5) 多名客戶一起，同時在不同分行進行大額現金交易；(6) 假鈔或偽造的金融票據；(7) 定期向高風險地區付款，或從高風險地區收款，而且款額大，又沒有明確的真正交易基礎。', 'The remaining four are: (4) numerous transactions, especially over a short period, each below the CDD threshold or not substantial on its own, but substantial in aggregate, or already over the threshold; (5) customers acting together to make simultaneous large cash transactions at separate branches; (6) counterfeit notes or forged financial instruments; and (7) regular large payments to or from higher-risk jurisdictions, without clear genuine underlying transactions.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第7.10(b)段', '¶7.10(b)', 'Cash transactions'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('三、貿易洗錢：十一項', '3. Trade-based laundering: eleven indicators', [
        ('第三組是貿易洗錢，共十一項。前四項是：(1) 高風險的起點或目的地；(2) 高風險貨物，例如高價而體積小的貨物（如電子產品），以及周轉快而且難以估值的軍民兩用貨物；(3) 提單或發票上的貨物描述，與實際付運貨物有重大差異；(4) 發票貨價與公平市場價值有重大差異。', 'The third group is trade-based laundering, and it has eleven indicators. The first four are: (1) a higher-risk origin or destination; (2) higher-risk goods, for example high-value, low-volume goods such as electronics, and dual-use goods with high turnover and valuation difficulties; (3) significant discrepancies between the descriptions on the bill of lading or invoice and the goods actually shipped; and (4) significant discrepancies between invoice values and fair market value.'),
        ('接下來四項是：(5) 交易規模與業務不符；(6) 付款方式增加風險，例如向高風險地區的新供應商預付款；(7) 無關的第三方付款；(8) 信用證被反覆延長或修改。', 'The next four are: (5) a size that is inconsistent with the business; (6) a payment method that increases risk, for example advance payment to a new supplier in a higher-risk jurisdiction; (7) unrelated third-party payments; and (8) letters of credit that are repeatedly extended or amended.'),
        ('最後三項是：(9) 交易方看似幌子或空殼公司；(10) 付運地點沒有合理理由，卻經其他地區轉運；(11) 付運的貨物不合經濟常理。第6部分「貿易洗錢」一節，另外說明文件24的四類指標；這兩套分類不要混成同一份清單。', 'The last three are: (9) trading parties who appear to be front or shell companies; (10) trans-shipment through other locations without justification; and (11) shipments that make no economic sense. The trade-based money-laundering section of this Part separately explains document 24’s four indicator groups. These are distinct lists, and must not be merged into one.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第7.10(c)段及註62–63', '¶7.10(c); footnotes 62–63', 'the use of an advance payment for a shipment'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('四、其他類型交易：七項', '4. Other types of transactions: seven indicators', [
        ('第四組是其他類型的交易，共七項。前四項是：(1) 活動與年齡、職業或收入不符；(2) 交易涉及據報與恐怖活動或指定恐怖分子有關的司法管轄區或實體；(3) 經常更改地址或獲授權簽署人；(4) 向衝突區的慈善或非牟利組織，或在與恐怖活動有關地區營運的組織捐款。', 'The fourth group is other types of transactions, and it has seven indicators. The first four are: (1) activity inconsistent with age, occupation or income; (2) transactions involving jurisdictions or entities reported to be associated with terrorist activities or designated terrorists; (3) frequent changes of address or authorised signatories; and (4) donations to charities or non-profit organisations in conflict zones, or to organisations operating in areas associated with terrorism.'),
        ('其餘三項是：(5) 用虛假資料或第三方，掩飾付款人或收款人；(6) 向避稅天堂，或與犯罪活動或高風險業務有關的地區反覆付款，或從這些地方收款，金額未必很大；(7) 與正常業務不符、又沒有明顯經濟理由，而匯至或來自高風險地區。', 'The remaining three are: (5) false information or third parties used to conceal payers or recipients; (6) repeated payments to or from tax havens, or areas associated with crime or high-risk business, and the amounts need not be large; and (7) unexplained transfers to or from higher-risk jurisdictions that are inconsistent with normal business.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第7.10(d)段', '¶7.10(d)', 'other types of transactions'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('五、代理／對手：四項', '5. Agents/counterparties: four indicators', [
        ('第五組是代理或對手，共四項：(1) 不願提供客戶識別資料；(2) 相較同區其他代理或對手，有大量大額或可疑交易；(3) 同一客戶的大量交易中，多次出現不同的姓名拼寫、虛假地址，或識別資料一部分改變、一部分維持不變；(4) 同一客戶在同一日，向多個代理或對手地點傳送資金，並聲稱是給同一或不同收款人。', 'The fifth group is agents or counterparties, and it has four indicators: (1) reluctance to provide customer identification information; (2) a high volume of large or suspicious transactions compared with other local agents or counterparts; (3) a large volume for one customer, with repeated different name spellings, false addresses, or identification that changes in part while other parts remain the same; and (4) funds sent by the same customer on the same day to several agent or counterpart locations, purportedly for the same or different recipients.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第7.10(e)段', '¶7.10(e)', 'agents or counterparts of MSO'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('六、客戶行為：五項', '6. Customer behaviour: five indicators', [
        ('第六組是客戶行為，共五項：(1) 由保持低調或在外等候的人陪同，或對提供資料顯得猶豫；(2) 催促完成交易，並承諾之後才補交文件；(3) 不在乎手續費或匯率；(4) 多名客戶看似合作，把一項交易拆成兩項或以上低於門檻的交易，以規避申報要求；(5) 不能為交易提供合理解釋。', 'The sixth group is customer behaviour, and it has five indicators: (1) companions who keep a low profile or wait outside, or a customer who hesitates to provide details; (2) urgency to transact, with documents promised later; (3) no interest in charges or exchange rates; (4) customers who appear to cooperate in splitting one transaction into two or more below-threshold transactions, in order to avoid reporting requirements; and (5) inability to justify the transaction.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第7.10(f)段', '¶7.10(f)', 'customer’s behaviour'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
])
